47
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:14,120
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Thank you, ComSec.

48
00:03:14,820 --> 00:03:18,020
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Again, magandang hapon po sa ating mga kasamahan

49
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:21,240
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: sa Kongreso at sa pamunuan at mga kawani

50
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:23,420
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: ng Department of Migrant Workers.

51
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:27,240
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Since its establishment in February 2022,

52
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:31,260
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: the DMW has been entrusted with a vital mandate

53
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:34,600
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: to protect the rights, promote the welfare,

54
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:38,440
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: and advance the interests of our overseas Filipino workers.

55
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:44,020
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Our OFWs continue to make a significant contribution

56
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:45,340
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: to our economy.

57
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:50,360
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: In 2025, OFW remittances reached a record

58
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:53,700
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: of 35.63 billion U.S. dollars,

59
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:57,120
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: 3.3% higher than the previous year.

60
00:03:57,700 --> 00:04:01,800
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: These remittances account for nearly 8% of our GDP

61
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:06,000
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: and underscore the important role of our migrant workers

62
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,480
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: as pillars of the Philippine economy.

63
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:13,280
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: For fiscal year 2027, the DMW is proposing

64
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:17,100
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: a budget of 10.675 billion pesos,

65
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:22,960
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: equivalent to only 0.23% of the national government's proposed budget.

66
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:27,280
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: The budget will support the operations of 42

67
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:29,240
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: migrant workers’ offices worldwide,

68
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:34,160
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: DMW regional offices, and OWA regional offices.

69
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:39,000
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: It will also strengthen the 2 billion peso Action Fund,

70
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:43,140
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: which provides legal, medical, repatriation,

71
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:45,780
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: and other assistance to OFWs,

72
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:52,800
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: as well as the 978 million peso Emergency Repatriation Fund

73
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:57,580
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: for workers affected by conflicts, pandemics, calamities,

74
00:04:57,660 --> 00:04:58,720
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: and other emergencies.

75
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:03,120
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: The budget will likewise support key programs,

76
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:07,480
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: including the OFW Hospital, National Reintegration Centers,

77
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:10,860
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: and Maritime Research Services.

78
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:15,180
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: As the Department continues to mature as an institution

79
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:18,320
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: under Republic Act No. 11641,

80
00:05:18,660 --> 00:05:21,880
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: we must ensure that it is adequately equipped

81
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:25,480
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: to fully carry out the provisions of the law.

82
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:29,460
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: As mandated, to create a reorganization commission

83
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:33,200
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: that will evaluate accomplishments and impact

84
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:34,800
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: of the DMW Act.

85
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:39,040
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: At this point, I believe the Department has demonstrated

86
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:41,960
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: its commitment to fulfilling its obligation

87
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:46,580
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: and providing our OFWs with protection, assistance,

88
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:48,800
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: and services they deserve.

89
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:53,900
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: I myself, as representative of the 2nd District of Zamboanga del Norte,

90
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:55,800
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: witnessed this commitment,

91
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,980
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: in the Department's swift response

92
00:05:57,980 --> 00:06:01,920
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: to the tragic case of our OFW constituent

93
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:03,340
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: who was slain in Lebanon.

94
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:06,500
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: In that difficult and heartbreaking situation,

95
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:11,260
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Secretary Cacdac himself personally attended to the case,

96
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:15,300
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: delivered the remains of our kababayan back to their grieving family,

97
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:17,800
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: and preserved her dignity

98
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:20,580
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: until she was brought to her final resting place.

99
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:22,740
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: This only comes to show

100
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:24,620
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: that the Department understands

101
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:28,920
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: that behind every OFW case is a human being,

102
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:31,360
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: a family, and a community

103
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:33,520
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: waiting for government to act.

104
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:36,060
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Our OFWs are truly

105
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:39,300
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: the makabagong bayani ng ating panahon.

106
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:41,700
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: It is therefore our responsibility

107
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:44,680
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: to ensure that when they leave our shores

108
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:47,300
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: to build a better future for their families,

109
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:49,780
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: they know that the Philippine government

110
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:51,560
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: will always stand behind them.

111
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:53,160
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Maraming salamat po.

112
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:57,640
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: At this time,

113
00:06:57,720 --> 00:06:59,240
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: I would like to recognize

114
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,040
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: the chairperson of the Committee on Overseas Workers' Affairs,

115
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:06,620
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Honorable Bryan Revilla

116
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:08,360
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: from the AGIMAT Party-list

117
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,680
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: to give his opening statement.

118
00:07:10,340 --> 00:07:12,540
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Madam Chair Irene Labad-Labad,

119
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:15,320
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: maraming salamat po sa aking mga kasama

120
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:15,960
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: dito po sa

121
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:17,440
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Committee of Appropriations.

122
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,580
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Distinguished guests,

123
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:19,740
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Mr. Secretary,

124
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:22,820
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: sa lahat po ng resource persons ngayong araw na ito,

125
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,960
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: magandang hapon po sa inyong lahat.

126
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:29,200
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: As chairman of the Committee on Overseas Workers' Affairs,

127
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:30,820
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: my mandate is clear.

128
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:33,860
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Ensure that the DMW and OWA

129
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:36,760
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: have the resources to protect and support

130
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:39,420
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: our OFWs in every circumstance.

131
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:42,000
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Not only when crisis strikes,

132
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:44,320
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: but in the ordinary days

133
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:46,140
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: when preparations matters most,

134
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:48,140
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: and in the difficult days

135
00:07:48,140 --> 00:07:49,520
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: when recovery begins.

136
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:52,060
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: The continuing Middle East conflict

137
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:54,200
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: has shown us why this matters.

138
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:56,800
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Thousands have been repatriated,

139
00:07:56,940 --> 00:07:59,040
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: placing significant demands

140
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:01,660
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: on DMW and OWA.

141
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:03,200
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: This year,

142
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:04,300
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: the government provided

143
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:06,340
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: an additional three billion

144
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:07,420
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: for the Action Fund,

145
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:09,640
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: while OWA received one billion

146
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:10,960
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: in supplemental funding,

147
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,940
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: including seven hundred million

148
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:14,760
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: for emergency repatriation.

149
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:17,000
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: But the question remains,

150
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:20,500
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: how far can these funds truly go,

151
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,360
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: and are they enough

152
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:24,100
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: for whatever crisis

153
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:24,980
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: comes next?

154
00:08:25,970 --> 00:08:28,540
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: But our responsibility to our OFWs

155
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:31,660
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: does not begin and end with a crisis.

156
00:08:32,350 --> 00:08:33,900
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: I have personally seen

157
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:38,120
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: our DMW and OWA perform

158
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:40,060
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: and serve our kababayans,

159
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:43,100
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: especially in the OFW Servicio Caravan.

160
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:46,040
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Having participated in a few of them,

161
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:47,940
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: these initiatives bring

162
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:49,620
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: frontline government services

163
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:52,400
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: directly to our OFWs on-site.

164
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:54,540
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Saving them time, money,

165
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,040
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: and the difficult choice

166
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:58,100
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: between accessing government assistance

167
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:00,160
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: and reporting for work.

168
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,940
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: This is the kind of service

169
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:03,480
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: that meets our OFWs

170
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,560
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: where they are.

171
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:06,800
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: And if we want to bring these services

172
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:08,640
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: to more Filipinos abroad,

173
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:12,180
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: then we must also make sure

174
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:14,220
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: that the DMW and OWA

175
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:16,300
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: have the resources to sustain

176
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:17,680
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: and expand them.

177
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:19,380
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: The question, therefore,

178
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:21,300
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: is not simply how much

179
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:22,160
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: has been spent

180
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:23,700
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: or how much remains.

181
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:25,500
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: The real question is

182
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:26,920
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: whether we are giving

183
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:29,900
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: DMW and OWA enough resources

184
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:32,140
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: to protect our OFWs

185
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:34,400
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: not only in the moments of crisis

186
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,100
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: but every day

187
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:37,600
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: in every circumstance.

188
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:39,120
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: And finally,

189
00:09:39,260 --> 00:09:41,280
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: we have to look beyond today's crisis

190
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,700
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: because Madam Chair,

191
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:45,080
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: this is not simply about

192
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:46,720
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: adding numbers to a spreadsheet.

193
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:49,060
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Hindi natin hinihingi

194
00:09:49,060 --> 00:09:50,420
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: ang karagdagang pondo

195
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:51,680
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: para lamang masabing

196
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,720
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: may pondo tayo.

197
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,880
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Hinihingi natin dahil may

198
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:57,280
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: mga Pilipinong umaasa na

199
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:58,760
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: kapag dumating ang oras

200
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,660
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: ng kagipitan, handa ang

201
00:10:00,660 --> 00:10:02,240
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: kanilang pamahalaan.

202
00:10:03,340 --> 00:10:05,880
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: If our OFWs can go

203
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:08,820
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: thousands of miles away from home,

204
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:10,280
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: from their families,

205
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:12,040
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: and our nation,

206
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:13,760
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: the least we can do

207
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:15,840
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: is go the extra mile for them.

208
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:17,700
Rep. Bryan B. Revilla: Maraming salamat po, Madam Chair.

209
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:20,820
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Thank you,

210
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:22,380
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Honorable Revilla.

211
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:24,900
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Now I would like to recognize

212
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:27,640
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: our co-sponsor

213
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:30,480
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: for the DMW budget,

214
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,940
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: our Honorable Representative

215
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:35,440
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: from Bohol First District,

216
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:37,320
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Congressman Baba Yap.

217
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:39,260
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Thank you, Honorable Chair.

218
00:10:39,420 --> 00:10:40,120
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Good afternoon,

