President Bongbong Marcos (video): May kabuhayan para sa hanap buhay, kaalaman para sa bagong kakayahan, kalinga para sa kapakanan at kaagapan para maiugnay sa mga servisyo.

749
00:31:53,740 --> 00:32:07,680
President Bongbong Marcos (video): serbisyong kailangan. May puhunan, may skills, may pagkakataong makabalik sa profesyon o makapagtayo ng sariling kabuhayan. At hindi nawawala ang serbisyo sa pagitan ng mga yugto.

750
00:32:07,880 --> 00:32:21,240
President Bongbong Marcos (video): Naroon ito kung saan naroon ang OFW. Bago umalis, habang nasa abroad, sa oras ng krisis, sa pag-uwi, naroon ang pamahalaan upang maglingkod.

751
00:32:22,010 --> 00:32:24,000
President Bongbong Marcos (video): Sa ating pagkakaisa at pagtututunan.

752
00:32:24,980 --> 00:32:37,240
President Bongbong Marcos (video): Mapapanatili natin ang katatagan ng ating bansa. At maisusulong ang isang mas maunlad na kinabukasan para sa lahat sa ilalim ng isang bagong Pilipinas.

753
00:33:10,920 --> 00:33:30,720
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: A couple of minutes, Madam Chair, to highlight. In accordance, if there's a review of our NEP, our Secretary mentioned po kung gaano kaimportante ang Emergency Repatriation Fund. Ito po'y sa OWA at ang Action Fund naman po sa DMW.

754
00:33:31,600 --> 00:33:41,140
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Sa NEP po namin, alos tatlong taon po na nasa 1.2 billion po ang Emergency Repatriation Fund po ng OWA.

755
00:33:41,800 --> 00:33:57,380
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito po ang pumupondo sa mga tickets, international, local. Patuwang ang Action Fund. At kasama rin po dyan po yung mga airport assistance, financial assistance, medical repatriation po para sa ating mga kababayan.

756
00:33:57,800 --> 00:34:06,740
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Everything related to repatriation. Ngunit sa NEP po namin ngayong taon, nabawasan po ito ng halos 300 million.

757
00:34:07,600 --> 00:34:27,020
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: So, ito po ay nasa 900 million level, Madam Chair. Ngayon po na nasa gitna pa rin po tayo ng regional conflict at hindi lamang naman po sa gitnang silangan merong existing na nangyayaring gulo na apektado po ang ating mga OFWs.

758
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:36,480
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yan ho siguro para mailapit. Ang unang-una pong gusto naming ilapit po sa Kongreso.

759
00:34:36,480 --> 00:34:47,260
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Dahil napaka-importante po nito. Minsan po may taon na hindi ho ito mayuutilize. Nagpapasalamat ho tayo kung hindi ho ito mayuutilize.

760
00:34:47,260 --> 00:34:52,960
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ibig sabihin, walang digmaan, walang pandemya, walang masamang nangyayari.

761
00:34:53,460 --> 00:35:04,840
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ngunit may taon, katulad ng taon ito, na on the part of the ERF of OWA po, we are running already on the supplemental na hiningi po namin, additional 700.

762
00:35:06,320 --> 00:35:16,700
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Including po yung lahat po na-utilize na, nasa 1.7 billion na po dahil sa nangyaring digmaan sa rehiyon.

763
00:35:18,120 --> 00:35:28,000
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: At ito po ay inaasahan namin na sana po ay mabigyan po kami ng additional budget sa Emergency Repatriation Fund.

764
00:35:28,480 --> 00:35:35,200
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito po ang cost of being ready ng gobyerno sa kung ano man po pwedeng mangyari sa ating mga OFWs.

765
00:35:35,820 --> 00:35:36,900
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Nasabi rin po ni,

766
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:45,960
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: na nabawasan po ang aming gas. Literally, we ran out of gas ang dating po.

767
00:35:47,260 --> 00:35:50,800
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Pwede ko po bang masabi rin kung bakit ito importante?

768
00:35:51,200 --> 00:36:01,220
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Kami po ay napaalalahanan ng COA na kailangan po ay itama natin or i-update natin ang sweldo ng mga JOs po.

769
00:36:01,980 --> 00:36:06,460
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Para po may konteksto, sa 1,600 po.

770
00:36:07,380 --> 00:36:15,240
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: One power complement po ng OWA, 1,100 po ay JOs or over 60 percent, close to 70 percent.

771
00:36:16,520 --> 00:36:22,880
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Malaki pong tulong sila sa amin habang pong inaayos natin ang karagdagang plantilya positions.

772
00:36:23,480 --> 00:36:32,640
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Madam Chair, overseas plantilya positions of OWA, ibig sabihin po ang mga welfare officers namin, AS, 34 lang po.

773
00:36:32,640 --> 00:36:37,120
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Kaya humihingi po kami ng karagdagang plantilya positions.

774
00:36:37,120 --> 00:36:44,940
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Kasi ayon po sa batas, creating the Department of Migrant Workers, katuwang po kami ng mga labor attache sa abroad.

775
00:36:45,520 --> 00:36:50,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Sa masamang pala do, hindi yung lahat ng post, meron pa po kaming welfare officer.

776
00:36:50,180 --> 00:36:59,240
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Dahil po ay kinukuha na nga rin po namin sa central office at sa mga regional office, nagkakaroon po na rin ng pagkukulang ng tao.

777
00:36:59,240 --> 00:37:03,320
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Kaya napaka-importante po ng aming mga JOs.

778
00:37:03,320 --> 00:37:06,240
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: At kung may ganun pong pag-a...

779
00:37:09,180 --> 00:37:17,580
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: abiso ang COA na itaas at iayon sa current rates ang sweldo ng JO, supportado po ito ng management ng OWA.

780
00:37:17,580 --> 00:37:25,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: At sana po, Madam Chair, mabigyan kami para naman po sulit na sulit ang kanila pong pagtatrabaho.

781
00:37:25,180 --> 00:37:30,840
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Sila po ay halos, ang operations po namin ng DMW ay 24-7 po, Madam Chair.

782
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:36,840
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: At ang pangatlo po, ay noong 1995 po, under Republic Act,

783
00:37:36,840 --> 00:37:39,600
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: 8042, ito po ang Migrant Workers Act.

784
00:37:39,600 --> 00:37:41,240
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito ho nagsimula ang lahat.

785
00:37:41,240 --> 00:37:48,840
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Meron ho ditong tinayo, ganun pa lang ho, siguro mga 30-31 years ago po.

786
00:37:48,840 --> 00:37:53,720
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ang tawag po dito ay Congressional Migrant Workers Scholarship Program.

787
00:37:54,440 --> 00:38:00,820
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito po ay scholarship program para sa mga anak ng OFWs at mga OFWs mismo po.

788
00:38:01,060 --> 00:38:06,480
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Kung susumahin, halos 60,000 po per year at apat na taon po.

789
00:38:06,600 --> 00:38:08,740
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yan po ang naibibigay na scholarship.

790
00:38:09,620 --> 00:38:16,420
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito po ay iba doon sa scholarship program ng OWA na pinupondohan ng trust fund o ibilang benepisyo.

791
00:38:17,320 --> 00:38:24,880
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ngunit, since 1995 po, nung nagbigay ang Kongreso po ng 50 million noon,

792
00:38:25,080 --> 00:38:27,300
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: hindi na po ito nabigyan ng pondo.

793
00:38:28,140 --> 00:38:35,420
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Gusto po sana namin din na hindi lamang po palakasin ito, lalo pong maramdaman ang ating mga kababayan.

794
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:36,540
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Dahil po,

795
00:38:36,540 --> 00:38:42,240
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: sa pananaw po namin, isa, if not, the major reason why our OFWs go abroad

796
00:38:42,240 --> 00:38:45,700
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ay para suportahan po ang pag-aaral ng kanilang mga anak.

797
00:38:45,900 --> 00:38:51,020
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: So with this po, may I add as well, that when it comes to scholarships po,

798
00:38:51,160 --> 00:38:57,160
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ang OWA po ay meron ng 20,000 scholars na mga anak ng mga OFWs.

799
00:38:57,300 --> 00:39:00,940
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: At sa suporta po ng aming mahal na Secretary at ng board,

800
00:39:01,100 --> 00:39:06,060
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: magdadagdag pa po kami ng 10,000 na scholarship slots for this year alone.

801
00:39:06,960 --> 00:39:13,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito pong congressional scholarship, madadagdaga na naman po kung ito po'y malalagyan ng pondo at mapapalakas.

802
00:39:14,020 --> 00:39:18,780
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: All in all po, alam po namin na limitado ang fiscal space.

803
00:39:19,580 --> 00:39:26,420
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ngunit, ang aming pong hiling ay huwag naman hong kalimutan ang ating mga OFWs, lalong-lalo na po,

804
00:39:26,540 --> 00:39:34,700
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: sila po ay araw-araw po yan, alam po ninyo, na humihingi ng tulong, yung iba po tulong ng repatriation,

805
00:39:34,920 --> 00:39:37,120
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: yung iba po tulong ng livelihood.

806
00:39:37,120 --> 00:39:43,100
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Pagdating dito, yung iba po tulong para po sa kanilang pamilya at kanilang mga anak.

807
00:39:44,360 --> 00:39:50,760
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Panghuli na po, katuwang po ng DMW, alam nyo naman po na under the Action Fund,

808
00:39:50,760 --> 00:39:54,640
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ay may kinukuha po tayong mga legal retainers abroad.

809
00:39:55,140 --> 00:40:00,860
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito po yung mga lawyers na nagtatanggol po sa ating mga OFWs.

810
00:40:00,860 --> 00:40:06,200
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Gusto po sana namin na magkaroon din ng medical retainers or clinic retainers,

811
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:15,080
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: dahil ayon po sa aming datos, ay dumami na po yung health concerns or medical concerns ng ating mga kababayan.

812
00:40:15,080 --> 00:40:24,900
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: And especially po, with special mention po, sa mga psychosocial counseling na kailangan ng ating mga kababayan,

813
00:40:25,020 --> 00:40:33,140
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: lalong-lalo na po, yung pong mga distress natin, especially po, malapit sa puso namin ang isekhans,

814
00:40:33,380 --> 00:40:35,040
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ang ating pong mga domestic workers.

815
00:40:35,040 --> 00:40:41,860
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Na talaga naman po nga, kailangan po nating tulungan at bigyang pansin.

816
00:40:41,860 --> 00:40:47,600
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yun lang po, Madam Chair, and we're open po, at baka meron pa pong mga tanong ang miyembro po ng committee.

817
00:40:47,780 --> 00:40:49,220
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Thank you very much po, Madam Chair.

818
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:54,660
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Thank you so much, OAA Administrator Patricia Yvonne Caunan.

819
00:40:55,960 --> 00:41:02,780
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Before we proceed with our interpolations, I would like to recognize our other members present here with us today.

820
00:41:02,780 --> 00:41:06,080
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: We have Vice Chair Agustina Dominique.

821
00:41:06,080 --> 00:41:07,420
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Ditse Tina Pancho.

822
00:41:07,560 --> 00:41:10,920
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Vice Chair Niko Raul Daza.

823
00:41:11,180 --> 00:41:13,700
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: And Vice Chair Maria Isabel Sagarbarria.

824
00:41:13,860 --> 00:41:15,380
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Good afternoon to everyone.

825
00:41:16,160 --> 00:41:19,960
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Now, we would like to open the floor for interpolations.

826
00:41:20,740 --> 00:41:28,160
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: May I remind our distinguished colleagues that each member is given five minutes for questioning or interpolation,

827
00:41:28,340 --> 00:41:31,460
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: excluding the response of the resource persons.

828
00:41:31,460 --> 00:41:34,520
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: And when you hear the bell sound, it means...

829
00:41:34,520 --> 00:41:38,340
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Wow.

830
00:41:38,340 --> 00:41:47,160
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: It means you only have 30 seconds to wind up with your questions.

831
00:41:47,500 --> 00:41:52,260
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: And as part of a long-standing and respected tradition of the House of Representatives

832
00:41:52,260 --> 00:41:57,140
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: to accord preferential treatment to the minority members of the House

833
00:41:57,140 --> 00:42:02,160
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: and followed by the independent and majority members in an alternating manner.

834
00:42:02,580 --> 00:42:06,020
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: So now, the Chair recognizes from the...

835
00:42:06,020 --> 00:42:06,700
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: The minority.

836
00:42:08,880 --> 00:42:12,400
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: First, we have Representative Dada Ismula.

837
00:42:14,180 --> 00:42:16,080
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat, Madam Chair.

838
00:42:16,640 --> 00:42:19,140
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Assalamualaikum warahmatullahi wabarakatuhu.

839
00:42:19,640 --> 00:42:25,500
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Magandang hapon po sa inyong lahat, Secretary Hans, at sa ating Administrator ng OWWA.

840
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:30,780
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Salamat po sa pagpunta ninyo and salamat po being our resource person.

841
00:42:31,180 --> 00:42:35,980
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At pagpapumanhin po in advance sa aking mga katanungan, ito po'y necessary.

842
00:42:35,980 --> 00:42:36,940
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Sige po.

843
00:42:36,940 --> 00:42:38,240
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Una po.

844
00:42:38,320 --> 00:42:45,260
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: It has been a year since the DMW raised the minimum wage of migrant domestic workers

845
00:42:45,260 --> 00:42:49,700
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: from 400 US dollar to 500 US dollar.

846
00:42:49,700 --> 00:42:56,160
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ano ang ginagawa po ng DMW to ensure the full implementation of this standard

847
00:42:56,160 --> 00:43:03,400
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: and ano rin po ang rate of compliance by countries of destination and recruitment agencies po?

848
00:43:04,640 --> 00:43:05,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes.

849
00:43:06,920 --> 00:43:07,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Magandang...

850
00:43:07,680 --> 00:43:12,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Araw pumulik, Congresswoman, Madam Chair.

851
00:43:13,040 --> 00:43:13,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes.

852
00:43:13,520 --> 00:43:20,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ang pagtalaga po ng 500 US dollar wage for our domestic workers

853
00:43:20,140 --> 00:43:27,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: was by virtue of the Department Order issued last August 2025, Department Order 25.

854
00:43:28,120 --> 00:43:35,620
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And since that time, ang sinagawa po natin ay bilang first phase ng ating implementation

855
00:43:35,620 --> 00:43:38,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: is on a voluntary basis.

856
00:43:40,120 --> 00:43:45,580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Since this will have implication on current contracts of OFWs,

857
00:43:45,580 --> 00:43:50,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ang ginawa po natin incentivization ang proseso na pinagdadaanan natin.

858
00:43:51,100 --> 00:44:00,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So we incentivize those who on their own provided domestic workers with a 500 US dollar salary per month.

859
00:44:01,240 --> 00:44:07,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sa ngayon po, we have 17,375 job orders processed.

860
00:44:07,040 --> 00:44:12,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: With a 500 US dollar salary for domestic workers.

861
00:44:12,720 --> 00:44:21,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And meron po tayong patuloy na pagpoprocess na mga job orders na ito.

862
00:44:21,660 --> 00:44:27,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ito po ay supplemented with other measures within the Department Order.

863
00:44:27,420 --> 00:44:35,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: For instance, we are braced to already implement yung tinatawag na video interview, yung know your employer.

864
00:44:35,440 --> 00:44:37,480
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Video interview.

865
00:44:37,480 --> 00:44:45,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Para po maisagawa yung mismong pagpapakilala ng domestic workers sa kanyang magiging future employer.

866
00:44:45,220 --> 00:44:46,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Para kilala na po niya.

867
00:44:46,880 --> 00:44:55,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So in this last quarter of 2026, we are braced to already fully implement itong video interview system.

868
00:44:56,680 --> 00:44:58,940
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ang isa rin pong sinasabi,

869
00:44:58,940 --> 00:44:59,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ang isa rin pong sinasabi,

870
00:44:59,420 --> 00:45:00,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Isa rin pong sinasagawa natin yung upskilling.

871
00:45:00,920 --> 00:45:06,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kailangan po kasing kasabayan ng pagpapatunay na may sapat na skillsets,

872
00:45:06,360 --> 00:45:10,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: skills being the highest form of protection ng ating domestic workers.

873
00:45:11,140 --> 00:45:17,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At sa ngayon po, we are undergoing projects, training ng mga domestic workers,

874
00:45:17,360 --> 00:45:23,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: turning them into other skillsets or skills options such as caregiving

875
00:45:23,280 --> 00:45:28,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and other types of skillsets in the restaurant sector, hospitality sector.

876
00:45:29,930 --> 00:45:35,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: For instance, meron tayong ilan who are in caregiving from Israel

877
00:45:35,520 --> 00:45:39,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: na na-i-place natin sa government-to-government hiring natin as hotel workers.

878
00:45:40,400 --> 00:45:47,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Some of them domestic workers also from the Middle East na naging hotel workers elsewhere,

879
00:45:47,740 --> 00:45:51,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: most especially sa mga government-to-government hiring partners natin

880
00:45:51,660 --> 00:45:54,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: sa Croatia.

881
00:45:55,720 --> 00:46:00,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ngayon, the other thing we are doing is pagbibigay ng livelihood options para sa kanila.

882
00:46:02,020 --> 00:46:08,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Marami po na tayong nabihayaan ng livelihood capital from the National Reintegration Center

883
00:46:08,760 --> 00:46:11,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: para hindi na sila mag-domestic work.

884
00:46:11,320 --> 00:46:14,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Dito na lang po nagtayo sila ng kanika nalang negosyo.

885
00:46:14,220 --> 00:46:20,640
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ang dami na po nating success stories, most notably, yung nag-business plan competition tayo,

886
00:46:20,640 --> 00:46:21,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ang top three winners.

887
00:46:21,600 --> 00:46:25,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ay mga puro former domestic workers.

888
00:46:25,500 --> 00:46:32,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So we are giving them options in terms of not just being domestic workers.

889
00:46:32,780 --> 00:46:34,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: There's nothing wrong with being a domestic worker.

890
00:46:34,960 --> 00:46:40,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: My own mother was a domestic worker when my dad lost his job as an OFW.

891
00:46:41,160 --> 00:46:47,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero kailangan lang meron options dapat ang ating mga kababayihang workers,

892
00:46:47,320 --> 00:46:51,620
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: especially that they are not just caught in a recruitment trap of just being,

893
00:46:51,620 --> 00:46:52,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: offered domestic work.

894
00:46:53,140 --> 00:47:00,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But the short answer to the question, ma'am, is we have 17,375 job orders processed

895
00:47:00,180 --> 00:47:03,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: with 500 US dollars salary and counting.

896
00:47:04,820 --> 00:47:10,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Aaminin ko, medyo naantala ang implementasyon natin gawa nitong krisis sa Middle East.

897
00:47:10,740 --> 00:47:16,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Nag-focus tayo sa repatriation effort at assistance measures na binibigay sa atin

898
00:47:16,600 --> 00:47:21,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: sa nanunumbalik na OFWs na, by the way, batay din sa datos ni Admin PY,

899
00:47:21,660 --> 00:47:26,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: around 30 to 40 percent, kung maalala ko yung huling pagtingin ko sa datos,

900
00:47:26,700 --> 00:47:28,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ay mga domestic workers.

901
00:47:28,360 --> 00:47:33,300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yung nanunumbalik doon sa 12,000 na napauwi natin ay karamihan domestic workers.

902
00:47:33,300 --> 00:47:37,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So it is still a work in progress, Madam Chair, Congresswoman Dada,

903
00:47:37,960 --> 00:47:43,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and rest assured we will continue to implement the 500 US dollar salary

904
00:47:43,540 --> 00:47:48,480
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: until it achieves a level of acceptability across the board

905
00:47:48,600 --> 00:47:51,640
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and then we can mandatorily impose the same.

906
00:47:52,320 --> 00:47:54,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Madam Chair, maraming salamat po.

907
00:47:55,300 --> 00:48:01,820
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Definitely understandable dahil sa naging conflict nga naman sa Middle East.

908
00:48:01,820 --> 00:48:07,680
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: So nagagalak ako na marinig na it is still ongoing up to the present na madagdagan pa

909
00:48:07,680 --> 00:48:14,480
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: at sana ay across the board na talaga na mataasan or ma-increase ang kanilang salary,

910
00:48:14,820 --> 00:48:17,780
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: lalong-lalo na yung mga domestic workers po natin.

911
00:48:18,520 --> 00:48:21,720
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Dadako naman po ako, Madam Chair, sa on-action.

912
00:48:22,700 --> 00:48:30,300
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ang agarang kalinga at saklolo para sa mga OFWs na nangangailangan o action fund

913
00:48:30,300 --> 00:48:38,080
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ay itinatag para mabigay ng timely and responsive services sa mga OFWs at kanilang mga pamilya.

914
00:48:38,540 --> 00:48:40,400
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Lalo na kapag sila ay nasa distress,

915
00:48:40,780 --> 00:48:47,840
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: pero meron pong ilang reports mula sa ground na mabagal ang disbursement ng financial support under action fund.

916
00:48:48,040 --> 00:48:51,260
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Madalas daw po ay umaabot ito ng 3 to 6 months

917
00:48:51,820 --> 00:48:52,460
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: kung ma-resolve ba.

918
00:48:52,640 --> 00:49:01,900
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: May mga kaso pa ng OFWs na namatay sa chronic illness habang naghihintay pa rin ng agarang kalinga at saklolo.

919
00:49:02,640 --> 00:49:06,200
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ano na po ang ginagawa para mabawasan ang red tape

920
00:49:06,200 --> 00:49:14,940
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: at mapabilis ang disbursement at case management system ng DMW para sa action fund at sa iba pa nitong programa po?

921
00:49:15,880 --> 00:49:20,840
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Madam Chair, with the permission, I will make an initial comment.

922
00:49:21,780 --> 00:49:27,060
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But Yusek Feli Bay can also supplement the answer.

923
00:49:27,280 --> 00:49:35,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But at the outset, let me say na 80,000, as I reported, 80,000 na po ang nabigyan ng financial assistance.

924
00:49:35,260 --> 00:49:42,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: However, tama po kayo, meron talagang hindi pa nabibigyan at meron na rin matagal-tagal nag-antay.

925
00:49:42,660 --> 00:49:47,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But the cause of this is once again, we don't use this as a common excuse

926
00:49:47,600 --> 00:49:51,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and I don't want to always get back to the crisis.

927
00:49:51,360 --> 00:49:52,200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: It's an excuse.

928
00:49:53,080 --> 00:49:58,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But ang nangyari po, yung 2 billion action fund natin na ubos po

929
00:49:58,360 --> 00:50:04,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: because of our massive repatriation and financial assistance distribution effort nung krisis.

930
00:50:04,400 --> 00:50:10,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Nung krisis, the height of it in March, April, May, yung US-Israel-Iran war,

931
00:50:11,800 --> 00:50:16,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ay 20,000 po ang nabigyan natin ng action fund assistance on the ground.

932
00:50:16,100 --> 00:50:21,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero malamang po kung dadaang you're referring to those who are here,

933
00:50:21,880 --> 00:50:22,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: who have returned.

934
00:50:22,600 --> 00:50:27,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So sa ngayon, naubos yung 2 billion, but as Yusef Niki mentioned,

935
00:50:27,540 --> 00:50:32,200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: no less than the President himself on June 23rd announced a 3 billion peso.

936
00:50:32,380 --> 00:50:37,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Hinigitan pa ni Pangulo yung 2026, yung 2025 budget.

937
00:50:37,800 --> 00:50:43,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: If it was 2 billion in 2025 as set in the 2026 GAA,

938
00:50:43,540 --> 00:50:46,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: sabi ni Pangulo, ang supplemental nyo, 3 billion.

939
00:50:46,820 --> 00:50:50,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So ongoing po ang distribution, rest assured.

940
00:50:52,160 --> 00:50:57,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Siyempre, mayroon lang usual COA procedures before we release,

941
00:50:58,080 --> 00:51:00,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: documentation of the releases.

942
00:51:01,080 --> 00:51:06,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: I wish we could just immediately unload the 3 billion that quickly,

943
00:51:06,260 --> 00:51:09,480
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: but rest assured, the releases are ongoing.

944
00:51:10,620 --> 00:51:14,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We post this naman po, at least some of the releases on our Facebook page

945
00:51:14,820 --> 00:51:18,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: just to make our people know that the releases are ongoing.

946
00:51:19,280 --> 00:51:21,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And rest assured po, makukompleto natin.

947
00:51:22,060 --> 00:51:26,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: The 3 billion peso allocation of the President himself is definitely enough

948
00:51:26,360 --> 00:51:30,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: to cover all the pending claims.

949
00:51:30,720 --> 00:51:36,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And rest assured, we will cover all the claims by the early 4th quarter, ma'am.

950
00:51:36,220 --> 00:51:37,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yung pending at least.

951
00:51:37,760 --> 00:51:40,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Maraming salamat, Madam Chair and Mr. Secretary.

952
00:51:41,380 --> 00:51:45,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At least po, ito'y maibibigay pa rin sa kanila.

953
00:51:45,720 --> 00:51:48,960
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And naintindihan po natin na because of the crisis din,

954
00:51:48,960 --> 00:51:51,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: at medyo late nga po yung mga downloads of funds.

955
00:51:51,720 --> 00:51:54,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Nga raw po ng mga iba-ibang departamento.

956
00:51:54,660 --> 00:51:58,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, most likely, baka isa din po yun sa tinitignan na dahilan.

957
00:51:58,980 --> 00:52:00,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kung bakit, nalilate din, no?

958
00:52:01,800 --> 00:52:04,200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: However, kaugnay nga po ng Action Fund,

959
00:52:04,500 --> 00:52:09,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: maari ko bang matanong ang ating ginoong sekretary na

960
00:52:09,180 --> 00:52:16,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: magkukumit ba po ang DMW na amyendahan ang Department Order 02-2025

961
00:52:16,760 --> 00:52:21,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: o omnibus guidelines on the implementation of the Action Fund

962
00:52:21,260 --> 00:52:26,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: para malinaw na ma-define ang ideal disbursement rate po.

963
00:52:27,840 --> 00:52:32,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes, right now, ang disbursement rates natin,

964
00:52:33,680 --> 00:52:39,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: generally speaking, are 50,000 for the distressed cases,

965
00:52:39,540 --> 00:52:43,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: 75,000 kapag merong medical situation,

966
00:52:43,820 --> 00:52:49,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and 100,000 kapag nasawi ang ating OFW sa kanasamaang palad.

967
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:52,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But yes, we are reviewing these rates kasi,

968
00:52:52,800 --> 00:52:56,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: meron din tayong quick action na tinatawag po eh.

969
00:52:57,310 --> 00:53:00,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, by way of example, pag may dumating na OFW,

970
00:53:00,540 --> 00:53:06,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: at ang case niya is not as major as the others,

971
00:53:06,020 --> 00:53:08,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: pero kailangan niya ng pamasahe, pauwi,

972
00:53:08,960 --> 00:53:11,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: kailangan niya ng pantawid kahit papano,

973
00:53:11,800 --> 00:53:18,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: may matutustos siya sa, halimbawa, bilang pocket money niya pauwi ng probinsya,

974
00:53:19,160 --> 00:53:22,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: then we have that quick action.

975
00:53:22,320 --> 00:53:29,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, we have a window where we provide 10,000 to around 5,000 to 10,000 to 30,000,

976
00:53:29,160 --> 00:53:30,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: depende dun sa need.

977
00:53:30,280 --> 00:53:33,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Dumbawa, abutan ng pamasahe, di 5,000, 2,000.

978
00:53:33,360 --> 00:53:38,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, but you're right, Mama, we need to rationalize and make sure that there is a definite schedule

979
00:53:40,000 --> 00:53:43,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: para malinaw po sa taong bayan kung ano yung saan na pupunta,

980
00:53:44,000 --> 00:53:47,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: saan na lalagay yung kanilang sitwasyon.

981
00:53:47,660 --> 00:53:52,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But there is another special rate which is around 30,000 pesos for the,

982
00:53:52,780 --> 00:53:54,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: traffic victims.

983
00:53:56,080 --> 00:54:00,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ito po yung mga either hindi nakaalis, illegal recruitment victims,

984
00:54:01,180 --> 00:54:07,000
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: or sila po ina-uwi, halimbawa, dun sa scam hub sa Southeast Asia.

985
00:54:07,340 --> 00:54:12,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, we have pegged the amount for them at 30,000 pesos.

986
00:54:13,360 --> 00:54:16,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, meron pong ganong klaseng differentiation lang tayo.

987
00:54:16,780 --> 00:54:20,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And you're right, we are reviewing the same, Madam Congresswoman,

988
00:54:20,340 --> 00:54:22,920
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and we'll issue the amendatory guidelines soon.

989
00:54:23,320 --> 00:54:26,100
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Salamat po, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary.

990
00:54:26,460 --> 00:54:28,760
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Dada ko naman po ako sa repatriation.

991
00:54:29,900 --> 00:54:36,540
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Base sa naging karanasan natin sa emergency repatriations dahil sa US-Iran conflict,

992
00:54:36,960 --> 00:54:40,840
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ano po kaya ang assessment ng DMW patungkol po dito?

993
00:54:40,840 --> 00:54:51,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes, ang assessment po natin, unang-una, may kahandaan po tayo at the outset

994
00:54:51,220 --> 00:54:52,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: kasi si Presidente po.

995
00:54:52,720 --> 00:54:58,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Unang-una niyang sinabi, day zero, kumbaga, Feb 28 kasi pumutok yung sigalot.

996
00:54:59,220 --> 00:55:03,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: May clear instructions na si Pangulo sa amin ni Sec. Tes. Lazaro ng DFA

997
00:55:03,680 --> 00:55:08,200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: to provide the welfare services for our OFWs.

998
00:55:08,200 --> 00:55:14,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At kami ni Admin PY, ang unang-unang naming naisip nung lumabas itong pumutok itong sigalot

999
00:55:14,740 --> 00:55:21,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: is yung mga masastranded gawa nung nasara yung airspace sa Gulf States, Dubai, Qatar, etc.

1000
00:55:22,520 --> 00:55:25,620
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So kami ni Admin PY, nagtungo kagad kami sa airport.

1001
00:55:25,620 --> 00:55:29,480
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Dahil alam namin magkakaroon ng embudo dun sa airport.

1002
00:55:29,480 --> 00:55:35,300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Dahil na-cancel ang flights, hindi na tuloy, and therefore may mga nasa labas ng airport

1003
00:55:35,300 --> 00:55:36,480
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: naging hintay ng tulong.

1004
00:55:36,480 --> 00:55:39,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So binigyan na ho namin ng agarang tulong and Admin PY could provide.

1005
00:55:39,680 --> 00:55:40,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: May data rin ho sila dyan.

1006
00:55:42,000 --> 00:55:47,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So that's one, the mechanisms, the systems.

1007
00:55:48,520 --> 00:55:52,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: On that particular day also, we met virtually all the ambassadors.

1008
00:55:53,260 --> 00:55:58,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sec. Tes. Lazaro and all the ambassadors on the ground with the labor attachés.

1009
00:55:58,440 --> 00:56:03,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Nagpulong na po kami lahat and activated our crisis manuals, crisis management systems.

1010
00:56:03,980 --> 00:56:08,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Existing na po ito. Marami nagtatanong kung meron bang ganito.

1011
00:56:09,080 --> 00:56:14,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Meron na po talaga, nakaabang na ito. So it's all a matter of activating these systems.

1012
00:56:14,280 --> 00:56:22,620
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And then, one key learning also is not all conflicts have the same size, so to speak.

1013
00:56:22,780 --> 00:56:26,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ibig sabihin na hindi one size fits all ang conflict.

1014
00:56:26,340 --> 00:56:35,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And this particular conflict is most, is kumbaga the best example of this principle.

1015
00:56:35,080 --> 00:56:39,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasi never pa ho nangyari na pitong bansa ang involved.

1016
00:56:39,480 --> 00:56:43,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Usually, when it's Israel-Lebanon, dalawang bansa lang po yan.

1017
00:56:43,160 --> 00:56:44,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Russia-Ukraine, dalawang bansa.

1018
00:56:45,430 --> 00:56:50,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But ito, covering yung theater of military operations, covered seven countries.

1019
00:56:50,340 --> 00:56:52,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And so that was the challenge.

1020
00:56:53,120 --> 00:57:01,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And we learned now, now, it's in our rule book, it's in our manuals, what to do kapag ganong karaming bansa

1021
00:57:02,040 --> 00:57:08,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ang literally involved sa drone attacks, missile attacks, dahil nandun nga rin po ang kababayan natin.

1022
00:57:08,360 --> 00:57:17,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So there was a learning experience, but at the same time, we needed to learn fast and apply our systems fast.

1023
00:57:17,300 --> 00:57:22,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So ang resulta nga po ay 12,000 ang nakauwi.

1024
00:57:22,600 --> 00:57:27,860
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: 12,000 na hindi nakauwi, pero nabigyan ng financial assistance.

1025
00:57:28,520 --> 00:57:31,920
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And the other learning is resources.

1026
00:57:32,180 --> 00:57:35,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So I'll go back to my point, ang point namin ni Admin PY.

1027
00:57:36,380 --> 00:57:46,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Talagang we need to have already, hindi, masasabi ko talagang hindi, I think Admin PY mentioned this already,

1028
00:57:46,140 --> 00:57:51,000
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: hindi po pwede talagang eksakto ang bit-bit namin sa bulsa namin.

1029
00:57:51,000 --> 00:57:57,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At the beginning of the year or at any given time, because anything can happen, as we all know.

1030
00:57:58,740 --> 00:58:03,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Unfortunately, the geopolitical situation is unpredictable.

1031
00:58:04,280 --> 00:58:12,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And so we must have the necessary resources, because we can and do mobilize such resources,

1032
00:58:12,460 --> 00:58:17,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and not just financial, I'm talking of material and human resource, when the time comes.

1033
00:58:17,820 --> 00:58:22,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Handa naman po tayo, but we just really need the proper resources in our hands.

1034
00:58:23,300 --> 00:58:25,320
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: I agree with that, Madam Chair.

1035
00:58:25,640 --> 00:58:29,960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At follow-up na lang po dyan, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary,

1036
00:58:29,960 --> 00:58:36,300
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: sa tingin niyo po ba may mga kailangang baguhin sa allocation, sa guidelines,

1037
00:58:36,620 --> 00:58:43,840
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: o kaya sa mga case management patungkol po sa pagiging mas responsive natin

1038
00:58:43,840 --> 00:58:49,360
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: at para mas maging sufficient din po ang pondo sa mga ganitong biglaang sitwasyon po?

1039
00:58:52,120 --> 00:58:53,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: I think, again,

1040
00:58:54,020 --> 00:59:01,580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: more than anything, yung financial resources, capabilities namin.

1041
00:59:01,760 --> 00:59:09,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Of course, yung human resources, dapat nakaabang, but that too is a function of our systems,

1042
00:59:09,300 --> 00:59:11,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: yung hiring processes and systems namin.

1043
00:59:12,080 --> 00:59:18,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: It's a good thing that before this conflict started, na-approve ng DBM on our part,

1044
00:59:18,320 --> 00:59:24,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: yung labing-labang additional items dun sa fund administration, action fund administration side.

1045
00:59:24,840 --> 00:59:31,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So nagpapasalamat kami kay Presidente sa DBM kasi nagkaroon ng fund management system yung aming action fund

1046
00:59:31,800 --> 00:59:35,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: before this all happened. So that was in place.

1047
00:59:36,760 --> 00:59:40,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And there were people who were dati kasi parang ad hoc task force lang,

1048
00:59:40,620 --> 00:59:44,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: but now there are really people and systems governing the action fund.

1049
00:59:45,220 --> 00:59:49,960
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Parang mini OWA, if I may say so, within the DMW that governs.

1050
00:59:49,960 --> 00:59:54,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kung trust fund ng OWA, kami naman governing the action fund.

1051
00:59:55,000 --> 00:59:57,620
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But again, I hate to be repetitive.

1052
00:59:58,140 --> 01:00:02,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But really, it's a matter of having the right resources.

1053
01:00:03,540 --> 01:00:08,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasi wala nang tatalo pa sa saying yes at the right moment.

1054
01:00:09,600 --> 01:00:15,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kesa sa ang sagot namin sa tao, ay pasensya na, wala kaming pondo.

1055
01:00:16,840 --> 01:00:23,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And we always need to be ready in terms of our financial systems.

1056
01:00:23,660 --> 01:00:28,940
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Now let me also add, na kami naman po are also in the process of enhancing our ISO systems.

1057
01:00:29,660 --> 01:00:35,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So on the part of the DMW and the OWA, we are geared to sharpen our ISO systems

1058
01:00:35,680 --> 01:00:40,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: para mabilis ang disbursement ng pondo, selection of our human resources,

1059
01:00:41,580 --> 01:00:45,860
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: mobilization of our human resources when the time comes.

1060
01:00:46,640 --> 01:00:50,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So right now, we're beefing up our human resources at the posts.

1061
01:00:50,880 --> 01:00:53,580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At dinadagdagan pa nga namin.

1062
01:00:53,580 --> 01:01:00,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ang aming mga posts, for instance, we recently opened our 43rd office in Cambodia.

1063
01:01:01,560 --> 01:01:05,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So ngayon, may tao na tayo nakaposition doon together working with our DFA

1064
01:01:05,780 --> 01:01:12,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: to respond to distress calls from our OFWs who are victimized by the scam hubs

1065
01:01:12,980 --> 01:01:16,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: or employed, unfortunately, by the scam hubs.

1066
01:01:16,520 --> 01:01:20,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So this is another learning that we've had.

1067
01:01:20,140 --> 01:01:22,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: It's always good to preposition our people.

1068
01:01:24,680 --> 01:01:27,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And that will probably be my final point.

1069
01:01:27,720 --> 01:01:31,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pagdating ng emergency, etong huling sigalot,

1070
01:01:31,600 --> 01:01:36,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: admin PY and I were able to preposition our people sa fly-out points.

1071
01:01:36,440 --> 01:01:38,640
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Not necessarily doon sa seven countries.

1072
01:01:38,880 --> 01:01:39,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sa labas nito.

1073
01:01:39,840 --> 01:01:42,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Para nakaabang nasa border, sundo, fly out.

1074
01:01:43,180 --> 01:01:47,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So ganon kahalaga rin yung resource, human and financial.

1075
01:01:47,540 --> 01:01:52,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Because dapat makabili kami kagad ng ticket, makabuo kami kagad ng augmentation teams

1076
01:01:52,660 --> 01:01:53,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: para nakapreposition.

1077
01:01:54,140 --> 01:01:59,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sa countries kung saan sasalubungin na yung lumalabas ng mga kababayan natin sa border.

1078
01:02:00,060 --> 01:02:00,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So yun po.

1079
01:02:01,240 --> 01:02:07,640
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: And I'm pretty sure, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary, na kapag bumibili kayo ng ticket on the spot,

1080
01:02:07,840 --> 01:02:10,040
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: napakamahal po ng mga ticket na ito.

1081
01:02:10,260 --> 01:02:13,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes. At hindi naman ho namin pwede sabihin sa inyo,

1082
01:02:13,280 --> 01:02:16,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: pasensya ho, hindi kami nakabili ng ticket kasi mahal.

1083
01:02:19,400 --> 01:02:19,920
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: That is true.

1084
01:02:19,920 --> 01:02:22,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Siguro pagagalitan nyo kami pag yan ang explanation naming sasabihin.

1085
01:02:23,040 --> 01:02:26,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Hindi kami umabot ng 12,000 kasi mahal ang ticket.

1086
01:02:26,700 --> 01:02:31,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero the good news is, umabot kami ng 12,000 kasi we just basically brought people home.

1087
01:02:31,520 --> 01:02:34,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: That was the main goal under the directive of the President.

1088
01:02:35,000 --> 01:02:37,960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: And we note, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary,

1089
01:02:40,060 --> 01:02:49,420
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: present po si Secretary Kakdak noong nagkaroon kami ng konsultasyon sa ating mga ilang mga OFW.

1090
01:02:49,860 --> 01:02:51,980
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Nagpapasalamat kami doon kay Secretary Hans.

1091
01:02:52,360 --> 01:02:54,000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Pero gusto lang.

1092
01:02:54,000 --> 01:02:58,340
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Kailangan po namin na put into record na hindi lahat ng mga kababayan natin po abroad,

1093
01:02:58,700 --> 01:03:01,420
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: which is na-mention naman po ni Secretary Hans kanina,

1094
01:03:01,540 --> 01:03:03,520
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ay gustong magpa-repatriate.

1095
01:03:03,820 --> 01:03:08,820
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: May mga ilang mga OFW po na nagre-request lang ng support for shelter

1096
01:03:08,820 --> 01:03:11,940
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: and other protective programs during the conflict.

1097
01:03:11,940 --> 01:03:17,420
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: We also agree with the OAPY statement earlier,

1098
01:03:17,420 --> 01:03:23,260
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: and that's why this representation would like to manifest that we support,

1099
01:03:23,260 --> 01:03:27,680
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: an increased budget for the Department of Migrant Workers and OWA.

1100
01:03:27,920 --> 01:03:32,700
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ngayon pa na may global conflict sa Middle East, ngayon pa talaga kayo binawasan.

1101
01:03:33,520 --> 01:03:39,620
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Kung saan maraming mga OFW, dapat mas palakasin at palawakin pa natin

1102
01:03:39,620 --> 01:03:43,260
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ang mga programang mag-aalaga sa ating mga kababayan abroad.

1103
01:03:43,620 --> 01:03:48,760
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Lalo pa sila po ang isa sa mga nangungunang nagpapatakbo sa ating ekonomiya.

1104
01:03:48,860 --> 01:03:50,680
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat po, Madam Chair.

1105
01:03:50,900 --> 01:03:53,720
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat po to the DMW family.

1106
01:03:57,340 --> 01:03:57,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes, go ahead.

1107
01:04:23,980 --> 01:04:25,620
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Take-home pay.

1108
01:04:25,620 --> 01:04:27,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So nagbigay tayo ng financial assistance.

1109
01:04:27,680 --> 01:04:29,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: 20,000 po yung naabutan natin noon.

1110
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:34,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And with admin PY, yung grocery food pack.

1111
01:04:34,240 --> 01:04:40,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So hindi lang financial, kundi basic food and shelter, and then—

1112
01:04:45,160 --> 01:04:45,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Temporary accommodation.

1113
01:04:46,440 --> 01:04:49,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Temporary accommodation, tama, shelters that we provide.

1114
01:04:49,700 --> 01:04:53,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasi nga po, ayaw nila umuwi.

1115
01:04:55,240 --> 01:04:56,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Temporary accommodation.

1116
01:04:56,240 --> 01:05:00,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero gusto muni nilang manirahan sa isang lugar kung saan they feel safe.

1117
01:05:00,420 --> 01:05:02,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And minsan pa, pinupuntahan pa na.

1118
01:05:02,360 --> 01:05:08,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At tapos kung may host country designated shelter, katulad ng Bahrain at Israel,

1119
01:05:08,800 --> 01:05:10,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: pinupuntahan ho namin sila doon.

1120
01:05:11,260 --> 01:05:15,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pinupuntahan namin sila doon sa government, host country government designated shelter

1121
01:05:15,280 --> 01:05:19,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: at inaabutan din ng tulong.

1122
01:05:19,420 --> 01:05:23,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So hindi ibig sabihin may host country government designated shelter,

1123
01:05:24,320 --> 01:05:25,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: hinahayaan na lang namin sila.

1124
01:05:25,540 --> 01:05:29,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pinupuntahan pa ho namin sila doon at binibigyan pa ng basic needs.

1125
01:05:31,580 --> 01:05:34,920
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Madam Chair, with your permission, just to add.

1126
01:05:38,500 --> 01:05:42,280
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yes, please proceed.

1127
01:05:42,280 --> 01:05:45,860
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Gusto ko lang pong klaruhin na yung aming emergency at repatriation assistance ng DMW at ng OWA,

1128
01:05:46,060 --> 01:05:49,940
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: hindi lang po kami taga-bili ng ticket, Madam Chair.

1129
01:05:50,660 --> 01:05:54,380
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yung ating pong rapid response team, yung minensyon po ni Secretary.

1130
01:05:54,380 --> 01:05:55,000
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yung rapid response team, yung minensyon po ni sekretary.

1131
01:05:55,000 --> 01:05:59,060
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Feb 28 po nagsimula ang gulo.

1132
01:05:59,060 --> 01:06:01,240
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: March 2 pa lang po nakapuesto na po.

1133
01:06:01,240 --> 01:06:03,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ngayon po siguro pwede nang sabihin.

1134
01:06:03,180 --> 01:06:13,140
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Sa border ng Egypt, sa Oman, sa Bahrain po, sa Kuwait, sa Qatar, sa Saudi, sa UAE,

1135
01:06:14,040 --> 01:06:19,420
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: nagpadala po tayo ng mga tao po dito at literal po,

1136
01:06:20,220 --> 01:06:23,680
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: tinutulungan pong makatawid from one border to the next.

1137
01:06:24,000 --> 01:06:31,160
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yung ating pong mga flights out of Oman, meron po doon kasama ang mga kababayan natin from UAE.

1138
01:06:31,820 --> 01:06:37,160
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Out of Riyadh, mga kababayan po natin from Kuwait, itinawid po natin.

1139
01:06:37,200 --> 01:06:43,260
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Bahrain, Qatar, at syempre sa eastern region rin po ng Saudi.

1140
01:06:43,740 --> 01:06:49,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito pong rapid response team po natin, of course, adopting a one country,

1141
01:06:49,180 --> 01:06:51,020
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: team approach with the DFA.

1142
01:06:52,480 --> 01:06:55,220
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Doon na po makikita yung iba't ibang assistance.

1143
01:06:55,780 --> 01:06:58,420
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Dito po napupunta yung pondo po.

1144
01:06:58,780 --> 01:07:03,840
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yung pong sa hotel nila, yung pong sa transportation, sa meals po nila,

1145
01:07:03,960 --> 01:07:09,240
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: hanggang po sa air tickets papuntang Maynila,

1146
01:07:09,300 --> 01:07:14,800
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: hanggang pong ticket po nila pauwing probinsya ay tinutulungan din po natin.

1147
01:07:14,800 --> 01:07:17,260
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: And on top of it, of course, Madam Chair,

1148
01:07:17,460 --> 01:07:23,080
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ang financial assistance po na ibinibigay po natin ng DMW at saka ng OWA.

1149
01:07:23,140 --> 01:07:27,540
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Napaka-importante po nitong RRT, yung sinasabi po ni SEC na personnel,

1150
01:07:27,860 --> 01:07:35,460
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: dahil po, kailangan pong i-augment yung ating pong mga teams abroad pag meron pong emergency.

1151
01:07:35,460 --> 01:07:40,480
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: So siguro, yung po rin ang maidagdag po, matingnan natin kung paano po mas mapalakas

1152
01:07:40,480 --> 01:07:47,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: yung ating pong personnel abroad kasi po ay sila po ang talagang nag-aaral.

1153
01:07:47,240 --> 01:07:51,120
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Frontliners po, frontliners, lalong-lalo na po pag may emergency.

1154
01:07:51,120 --> 01:07:58,680
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Sila rin po naka-experience nung mga, kami po ni SEC, nung pumunta po kami ng Romania recently SEC,

1155
01:07:58,840 --> 01:08:07,960
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: dahil po doon sa naging conflict din po that were faced by RC Ferrer sa Black Sea,

1156
01:08:08,120 --> 01:08:13,340
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: nakakatanggap din po kami nung emergency warning for drone attacks.

1157
01:08:13,760 --> 01:08:18,240
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ganyan po ka-totoo ang emergency warning.

1158
01:08:18,300 --> 01:08:20,240
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ang nangyayari at yan po ay regular na na-experience.

1159
01:08:20,240 --> 01:08:25,760
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Hindi lang po ng ating mga OFWs, pati po ang ating mga deployed personnel po.

1160
01:08:25,880 --> 01:08:27,480
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Maraming salamat po, Madam Chair.

1161
01:08:29,360 --> 01:08:31,580
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Thank you, Honorable Dadah Ismula.

1162
01:08:32,280 --> 01:08:39,780
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Now, from the majority, the Chair now recognizes Representative Mica Gonzales.

1163
01:08:40,840 --> 01:08:42,360
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Thank you, Madam Chair.

1164
01:08:43,360 --> 01:08:45,780
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Thank you, Sec. Hans, for coming.

1165
01:08:45,780 --> 01:08:48,760
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: And also the OWWA family and the DMW family.

1166
01:08:49,180 --> 01:08:53,980
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: I just have a few questions on the reintegration program.

1167
01:08:54,700 --> 01:09:02,900
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Because from the previous hearing sa People's Center, I asked whether the people who asked for a repatriation,

1168
01:09:03,060 --> 01:09:06,180
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: do they have a chance to go back again to work?

1169
01:09:06,300 --> 01:09:09,140
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Kasi siyempre, kaya nga sila nag-abroad kasi gusto nila magtrabaho abroad.

1170
01:09:09,140 --> 01:09:14,680
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: But given the situation, they cannot continue working there because of the conflict.

1171
01:09:15,040 --> 01:09:23,680
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: So I would like to ask on the update on the reintegration program doon po sa umuwi from Middle East to the Philippines.

1172
01:09:26,560 --> 01:09:27,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes po.

1173
01:09:28,080 --> 01:09:30,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And salamat po sa tanong.

1174
01:09:30,500 --> 01:09:36,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And yes, this is a foremost directive and concern also of no less than the President.

1175
01:09:37,120 --> 01:09:43,580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So ang sinagawa po natin, unang-unang step po doon is the profiling of those who had returned.

1176
01:09:43,880 --> 01:09:47,000
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So we need to know who they are, what their skill sets are.

1177
01:09:47,160 --> 01:09:50,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And whether or not they have an intent to return.

1178
01:09:50,440 --> 01:10:02,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: A vast majority, based on the profile tools, yung digital profiling na ginawa ng OWWA at ng DMW, want to stay.

1179
01:10:02,460 --> 01:10:10,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So dito po sa vast majority who want to stay, of the 12,000 po, roughly mga 9,000 were OFWs.

1180
01:10:11,680 --> 01:10:16,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: 3,000 of the 12,000 were dependents of OFWs.

1181
01:10:16,160 --> 01:10:23,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Mga anak po, kasi OFWs naman usually will bring their children or dependents and they will not go home without their children and dependents.

1182
01:10:23,240 --> 01:10:28,920
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So of the 9,000, nagkaroon po tayo ng intervention sa kanila.

1183
01:10:28,940 --> 01:10:31,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We knew who they were coming in.

1184
01:10:31,760 --> 01:10:42,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And nag-conduct po tayo ng around nearly 20 National Reintegration Network Job, Livelihood, and Skills Fairs.

1185
01:10:43,620 --> 01:10:52,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And dito po, una, aside from the job offers na binigay, nagkaroon din tayo ng active labor market interventions.

1186
01:10:53,600 --> 01:11:03,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ibig sabihin, based on their profiles, nalaman natin ang skill sets nila at hinanapan natin ng corresponding job orders overseas.

1187
01:11:05,160 --> 01:11:08,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Overseas po ito, wala pa dito yung DOLE side, yung local.

1188
01:11:08,160 --> 01:11:12,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So based on this framework, we had sent letters.

1189
01:11:12,900 --> 01:11:19,940
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Emails to the returning OFWs and told them, okay, you are a barista in UAE.

1190
01:11:20,060 --> 01:11:29,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ito ang mga job orders natin sa Asia and Europe and Americas pertaining to the job of being a barista.

1191
01:11:29,020 --> 01:11:31,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: This is an ongoing process.

1192
01:11:31,380 --> 01:11:39,200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So we had sent them emails and the ongoing process po ito, admittedly, hindi instant ang acceptance nila.

1193
01:11:39,200 --> 01:11:44,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But meron na po mga napaprocess for possible work overseas.

1194
01:11:44,900 --> 01:11:58,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: For those who wish to establish businesses, ang livelihood interventions naman po natin are through, of course, the DMW and OWWA reintegration funds,

1195
01:11:58,500 --> 01:12:08,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: but also DTI, Department of Trade and Industry, a Small Business Corporation, have their own loan facility, especially for returning women workers through Sec. Cris Roque.

1196
01:12:08,360 --> 01:12:17,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sec Kiko Laurel also has his own Department of Agriculture, Agribusiness Interventions, Startup Capital.

1197
01:12:18,420 --> 01:12:27,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sec. Dita of DOT, meron ding mga tourism-related businesses offered, among others.

1198
01:12:27,860 --> 01:12:30,480
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: DOST meron din, science and technology related.

1199
01:12:30,480 --> 01:12:38,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Now, sa skills enhancement, nandun din si Sec Kiko Benitez, DG Kiko Benitez at ang TESDA.

1200
01:12:38,540 --> 01:12:42,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, sa mga national reintegration fairs po namin, nandun yung mga agencies na binanggit ko.

1201
01:12:43,880 --> 01:12:56,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Tapos, nandun yung TESDA to offer skills-related certificates, training vouchers for the returnees.

1202
01:12:56,980 --> 01:13:04,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Tapos, meron pa ho itong 160 pesos stipend. Libre yung training, tapos may stipend pa yan daily pag natanggap sila.

1203
01:13:04,120 --> 01:13:07,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: By way of example, galing kami sa Naga.

1204
01:13:07,540 --> 01:13:09,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: With Mayor Leni.

1205
01:13:09,840 --> 01:13:22,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At doon, merong mga 25 na binigyan ng certificate to start their six-month AI course, AI-related course with STI.

1206
01:13:23,020 --> 01:13:24,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, we partnered with STI.

1207
01:13:25,220 --> 01:13:30,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So that’s just an example of doon naman sa skills-related part.

1208
01:13:30,700 --> 01:13:38,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Now, there would be around 30–40% in the category that you mentioned, Madam Congresswoman.

1209
01:13:38,920 --> 01:13:40,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yung mga gustong bumalik.

1210
01:13:40,620 --> 01:13:43,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ito naman po, meron na po rin pong nakabalik.

1211
01:13:44,060 --> 01:13:48,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasi it takes six months from the time they leave UAE, for instance.

1212
01:13:50,120 --> 01:13:53,620
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Buhay pa for six months yung kanilang valid employment visa.

1213
01:13:53,620 --> 01:13:56,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And they can just easily return to re-assume their jobs.

1214
01:13:58,820 --> 01:14:03,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Some were employed in businesses na talagang tumigil.

1215
01:14:03,340 --> 01:14:07,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, they are waiting for their businesses to resume.

1216
01:14:07,600 --> 01:14:12,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But some were able to already come back, to go back to the work that they have.

1217
01:14:12,900 --> 01:14:16,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: For instance, mga hotel workers at mga office workers.

1218
01:14:16,120 --> 01:14:19,200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Meron naman po sila rin nabalikan ng mga trabaho.

1219
01:14:21,160 --> 01:14:22,500
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Thank you, Madam Chair.

1220
01:14:22,500 --> 01:14:30,420
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: So, from what I understood, kapag po yung isang OFW yun na repatriate from the UAE back to the Philippines,

1221
01:14:30,580 --> 01:14:31,800
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: you offer two options.

1222
01:14:32,400 --> 01:14:37,280
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Whether they go back abroad, it may be Asia, it may be the Middle East or Europe,

1223
01:14:37,460 --> 01:14:39,840
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: or they can grow locally.

1224
01:14:40,660 --> 01:14:41,220
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Right?

1225
01:14:41,300 --> 01:14:42,080
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: So, I think okay.

1226
01:14:43,060 --> 01:14:44,740
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: That's the first question po.

1227
01:14:44,900 --> 01:14:48,240
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: The second question is about OFW Hospital.

1228
01:14:48,760 --> 01:14:53,740
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Because I represent po kasi third district of Pampanga and I cover San Fernando City, no?

1229
01:14:53,940 --> 01:14:57,580
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: So, I would like to ask because the last time I visited there,

1230
01:14:58,380 --> 01:15:01,120
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: there was a problem on the procurement.

1231
01:15:01,540 --> 01:15:02,760
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: So, ang tagal ng process.

1232
01:15:04,180 --> 01:15:06,880
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Yung mga pasyente, siyempre they cannot wait.

1233
01:15:07,120 --> 01:15:09,900
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: So, ang daming reklamang dumadaan that time.

1234
01:15:10,060 --> 01:15:16,760
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: So, I would like to ask from your office, Sec. Hans, or anyone from DMW,

1235
01:15:17,460 --> 01:15:20,080
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: ano na po ang status ng procurement process?

1236
01:15:20,400 --> 01:15:26,420
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: And number two, how’s the plantilla positions in OFW Hospital?

1237
01:15:27,200 --> 01:15:27,700
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Thank you.

1238
01:15:30,020 --> 01:15:31,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Okay po, ma’am.

1239
01:15:32,100 --> 01:15:40,860
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Meron tayong, on average, ongoing po yung procurement po at least on two major items.

1240
01:15:41,280 --> 01:15:47,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: One is yung sa medical supplies and one is on yung, should I say, the hard equipment,

1241
01:15:47,640 --> 01:15:52,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: yung mga medical machines such as CAT scans.

1242
01:15:52,120 --> 01:15:54,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And other types, X-rays, etc.

1243
01:15:55,580 --> 01:16:03,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, doon po sa medical supplies, we had substantially resolved the problem.

1244
01:16:03,200 --> 01:16:08,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: There used to be pagkukulang-kakulangan ng mga gamot sa pharmacy.

1245
01:16:08,340 --> 01:16:17,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But because we had partnered with a Philpharma group,

1246
01:16:18,060 --> 01:16:22,580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sina Usec. Kim, which is an adjunct,

1247
01:16:22,580 --> 01:16:27,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: of the DTI, yung pharma tie-up ng DTI,

1248
01:16:27,320 --> 01:16:32,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ay na-resolve na po ito kasi nagkaroon na ng steady delivery of medical supplies.

1249
01:16:32,740 --> 01:16:35,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So the challenge is mainly doon sa equipment.

1250
01:16:38,020 --> 01:16:45,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And one key development here is it took quite a while,

1251
01:16:45,760 --> 01:16:50,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But finally may sarili nang BAC, Bids and Awards Committee, ang ospital.

1252
01:16:50,120 --> 01:16:53,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: For a while, it was centralized with the DMW.

1253
01:16:54,160 --> 01:16:59,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But the problem there kasi is we needed to wait for the right moment

1254
01:16:59,740 --> 01:17:07,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: na na-position na yung mga regular employees that had been filled up.

1255
01:17:07,600 --> 01:17:14,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And the number we have is around 198, regular positions that we had filled up.

1256
01:17:15,000 --> 01:17:18,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Hinintay po muna namin sila mag-settle down upon hiring

1257
01:17:18,720 --> 01:17:23,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: para sila magkaroon na ng kumpiyansa at sistema sa kanilang procurement.

1258
01:17:24,040 --> 01:17:27,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, we had turned over procurement duties to the hospital.

1259
01:17:28,720 --> 01:17:30,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And this will go a long way.

1260
01:17:30,260 --> 01:17:35,580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: kasi mas, kumbaga obviously, mas autonomous sila at mas mabilis na silang umaksyon

1261
01:17:35,580 --> 01:17:39,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And ongoing po sa ngayon,

1262
01:17:39,020 --> 01:17:41,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ang review and posting,

1263
01:17:41,660 --> 01:17:47,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: 41.4% ongoing ang procurement,

1264
01:17:47,440 --> 01:17:50,640
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and 35.6% fully served.

1265
01:17:51,160 --> 01:17:52,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So work in progress.

1266
01:17:52,600 --> 01:18:01,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: yung 41.4% and the rest are still in the preliminary process.

1267
01:18:01,600 --> 01:18:04,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: hindi po... kasi iba-iba naman ang timelines.

1268
01:18:05,580 --> 01:18:07,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Still under process by the BAC.

1269
01:18:07,680 --> 01:18:15,860
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But at release, 77% of our procurement items had been acted upon.

1270
01:18:16,660 --> 01:18:20,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And the rest still under-processed yung paperwork sa BAC.

1271
01:18:20,280 --> 01:18:21,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But rest assured, ma'am,

1272
01:18:22,320 --> 01:18:23,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Bibilisan po natin ito.

1273
01:18:24,040 --> 01:18:29,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: You may be referring to the recent problem we had with our CAT scan.

1274
01:18:29,940 --> 01:18:31,940
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But this had already been resolved.

1275
01:18:32,100 --> 01:18:34,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We even sought the intervention of the Japanese authorities.

1276
01:18:35,020 --> 01:18:37,960
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasi galing sa Japan yung makina, yung equipment.

1277
01:18:39,060 --> 01:18:42,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, this had been recently resolved.

1278
01:18:42,560 --> 01:18:48,480
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And the key equipment part is now braced for delivery.

1279
01:18:49,740 --> 01:18:50,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And we will...

1280
01:18:50,740 --> 01:18:51,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ah, delivered na?

1281
01:18:51,800 --> 01:18:52,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Okay.

1282
01:18:53,020 --> 01:18:56,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So we are now braced to testing na

1283
01:18:56,980 --> 01:19:00,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and then we will now operate the CAT scan machine once again.

1284
01:19:00,520 --> 01:19:01,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, rest assured, ma'am.

1285
01:19:02,140 --> 01:19:07,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And then, merong MRI machine that is up for procurement.

1286
01:19:07,620 --> 01:19:16,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: With your permission, can I ask you, Sec. Nikki, so I don’t keep looking at her, to respond

1287
01:19:16,020 --> 01:19:18,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: to the MRI and other concerns.

1288
01:19:21,520 --> 01:19:23,620
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: With the permission of the Secretary, po.

1289
01:19:24,080 --> 01:19:24,860
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: Tama po.

1290
01:19:24,940 --> 01:19:28,520
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: Yung mga equipment po, critical equipment, have already been delivered.

1291
01:19:28,520 --> 01:19:33,820
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: And under procurement po ngayon yung mga gagamitin din po ng ating cancer care facility

1292
01:19:33,820 --> 01:19:42,640
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: which hopefully by first quarter or second quarter of 2027 ma-operationalize na rin po natin.

1293
01:19:42,840 --> 01:19:48,900
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: And on top of the plantilla positions mentioned earlier by the Secretary, we were given

1294
01:19:48,900 --> 01:19:51,580
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: additional 110 plantilla positions.

1295
01:19:51,580 --> 01:19:53,020
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: So that makes it around

1296
01:19:53,020 --> 01:20:01,860
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: 308 permanent plantilla positions under level 2 accreditation from the Department of Health.

1297
01:20:01,980 --> 01:20:07,780
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: And we continuously hire medical and administrative staff at the moment.

1298
01:20:09,700 --> 01:20:11,720
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Thank you. Thank you for those answers.

1299
01:20:12,820 --> 01:20:17,860
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Kasi po, I'm very into the OFW Hospital because I filed a bill

1300
01:20:17,860 --> 01:20:21,820
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: at approved na po ito sa Committee on Health to make it level 3.

1301
01:20:22,020 --> 01:20:25,140
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Kaya I'm very much concerned about OFW Hospital.

1302
01:20:25,140 --> 01:20:32,260
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: But on that note, of course, I fully support the manifestation of Kong Dadah to increase our budget.

1303
01:20:32,380 --> 01:20:37,200
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Kasi yung mga nandito nga sa Pinas, atat tayong tulungan, di ba?

1304
01:20:37,360 --> 01:20:40,300
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: What more yung mga nasa abroad na malayo sa pamilya.

1305
01:20:40,400 --> 01:20:49,260
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: So I think that's a point na kailangan nating make sure na they are catered for, they cared for,

1306
01:20:49,320 --> 01:20:51,160
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: and most importantly, dapat naramdaman nila.

1307
01:20:51,360 --> 01:20:53,500
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: So that's all, Madam Chair. Thank you very much.

1308
01:20:55,140 --> 01:20:57,300
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Thank you, Honorable Mica Gonzales.

1309
01:20:58,100 --> 01:21:03,340
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Now, from the minority, the Chair recognizes Honorable Robert Nazal.

1310
01:21:05,200 --> 01:21:06,580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you, Madam Chair.

1311
01:21:06,780 --> 01:21:09,040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Good afternoon to the DMW.

1312
01:21:09,280 --> 01:21:10,920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Good afternoon, Secretary Cacdac.

1313
01:21:11,100 --> 01:21:14,580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And good afternoon to the DMW family.

1314
01:21:15,920 --> 01:21:22,140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, I refer to the August 25, 2026 letter of...

1315
01:21:22,140 --> 01:21:27,860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: OWWA Administrator, Attorney Patricia Yvonne Caunan, requesting our support

1316
01:21:27,860 --> 01:21:33,400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: for an additional 2 billion in OWWA's fiscal year 2027 budget.

1317
01:21:34,040 --> 01:21:37,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, I am disappointed with the NEP.

1318
01:21:38,320 --> 01:21:44,780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: OWWA's total budget appears to increase by 1.48% because personnel services increased.

1319
01:21:45,420 --> 01:21:49,480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But MOOE was cut by 64.812 million.

1320
01:21:50,420 --> 01:21:52,920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Capital outlay by 72 million.

1321
01:21:53,440 --> 01:22:00,300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And the Emergency Repatriation Fund by 308.778 million, or 24%.

1322
01:22:02,980 --> 01:22:11,100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Now, my question is, Madam Chair, through the Chair, may I ask Administrator Caunan,

1323
01:22:12,100 --> 01:22:21,520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: OWWA proposed 12.8 billion, but only 4.3 billion was included in the NEP, despite the 8.533 billion gap.

1324
01:22:22,610 --> 01:22:25,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: OWWA is asking Congress to restore only 2 billion.

1325
01:22:25,890 --> 01:22:33,800
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Is this already the irreducible minimum for statutory life and safety and implementation-ready requirements?

1326
01:22:37,400 --> 01:22:40,060
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Madam Chair, with the permission of our Secretary,

1327
01:22:42,700 --> 01:22:50,960
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: At alam niyo po, siyempre po para sa OFWs, dapat itodo, Madam Chair, Cong.

1328
01:22:51,860 --> 01:22:58,740
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Lalong-lalo na po yung nasabi na po ni Sec. Hans, ito pong krisis paiba-iba.

1329
01:22:58,780 --> 01:22:59,780
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Meron po isang...

1330
01:22:59,780 --> 01:23:02,780
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: bansa lang, meron dalawang bansa.

1331
01:23:04,680 --> 01:23:08,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Sa Middle East crisis, pitong bansa, Madam Chair.

1332
01:23:08,180 --> 01:23:14,470
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: At hindi lamang naman yun ang krisis na dinadaanan ng ating mga kababayan.

1333
01:23:16,220 --> 01:23:25,620
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Marami din po tayong tinutulungan na medical repatriation at iba't ibang klase pong emergencies as defined.

1334
01:23:26,930 --> 01:23:29,580
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Alam niyo po, Madam Chair, nasabi ko kanina,

1335
01:23:29,600 --> 01:23:32,060
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: halos tatlong taon po tayong

1336
01:23:32,060 --> 01:23:34,980
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ang ERF ay nasa 1.2 billion.

1337
01:23:35,960 --> 01:23:43,160
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: At ngayong nasa gitna po tayo ng matinding, hindi pa ho tapos ang krisis ng US-Iran conflict.

1338
01:23:44,260 --> 01:23:47,140
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yung 900 million ho, Madam Chair, hindi sapat.

1339
01:23:48,340 --> 01:23:54,600
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ang hinihingi po namin, of course, at the very minimum po, i-restore yung 1.2.

1340
01:23:55,140 --> 01:24:00,040
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ngunit, siguro naman ho bilang administrator,

1341
01:24:00,720 --> 01:24:03,420
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: mandato ko rin ho talagang i-advocate.

1342
01:24:04,480 --> 01:24:08,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Currently po ang nagastos na po natin ay 1.7 billion.

1343
01:24:09,300 --> 01:24:14,580
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ibig sabihin ang amount na 1.2 or on the part of DMW na 2 billion.

1344
01:24:14,580 --> 01:24:20,780
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Pag may krisis na kasing laki ng hinarap po natin, Kong at Madam Chair,

1345
01:24:22,120 --> 01:24:24,920
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: tatlong buwan, anim na buwan, ubos na po agad.

1346
01:24:24,920 --> 01:24:29,260
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Pag po krisis, ang ticket po walang promo fare.

1347
01:24:30,000 --> 01:24:35,320
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ang ticket po nakatodo po, lalong-lalo na kung limitado ang tickets

1348
01:24:35,320 --> 01:24:39,000
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: at ang mga aeroplano, hindi po sila lumilipad.

1349
01:24:39,620 --> 01:24:48,000
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: So, when we asked Madam Chair for additional budget of 2 billion,

1350
01:24:48,240 --> 01:24:53,400
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: of which close to 600 million is for the emergency repatriation,

1351
01:24:53,400 --> 01:24:56,600
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: we were just looking at what currently,

1352
01:24:56,720 --> 01:25:01,320
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ay pinagdadaanan natin.

1353
01:25:02,900 --> 01:25:08,800
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: But aside from the Middle East crisis, there are other geopolitical conflicts

1354
01:25:08,800 --> 01:25:14,720
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: in other parts of the world, Madam Chair, even near us here in the Philippines,

1355
01:25:14,720 --> 01:25:20,980
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: that kailangan din po maging ready yung ating mga kababayan.

1356
01:25:20,980 --> 01:25:26,320
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: So, nung nag-propose po ang OWWA ng 12 billion po sa DBM,

1357
01:25:26,640 --> 01:25:32,700
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Limang billion po doon sa 12 ay para po sa emergency repatriation fund.

1358
01:25:33,600 --> 01:25:37,500
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ngunit, syempre po, naiintindihan natin the limited fiscal space,

1359
01:25:37,760 --> 01:25:43,140
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: naiintindihan po natin lahat, kailangan ng additional budget, kailangan ng tulong.

1360
01:25:43,960 --> 01:25:48,640
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ngunit, sa gitna ng pinagdadaanan natin ngayon, na hindi pa tapos na krisis, Madam Chair,

1361
01:25:49,460 --> 01:25:57,580
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ay hindi naman yata namin kakayanin na mas mababa pa po ang budget kesa noon na walang ganitong klaseng kaguluhan.

1362
01:25:57,800 --> 01:25:59,060
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yun po, Madam Chair.

1363
01:26:01,780 --> 01:26:07,660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, magkano po yung nagastos nyo before the crisis?

1364
01:26:08,380 --> 01:26:10,580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And how much did you spend after the crisis?

1365
01:26:11,300 --> 01:26:13,140
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Maganda pong tanong yan, Madam Chair.

1366
01:26:13,740 --> 01:26:20,660
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Normally po, for the last, I would say 2024 and 2025, out of the 1.2 billion,

1367
01:26:20,840 --> 01:26:24,780
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: so ibig sabihin po, walang aggravation ng regional conflict,

1368
01:26:25,140 --> 01:26:28,740
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Our utilization for the ERF was already

1369
01:26:28,740 --> 01:26:30,640
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: at 60%.

1370
01:26:32,700 --> 01:26:37,020
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ngayon po, noon nagkaroon ng krisis, naubos po yung 1.2,

1371
01:26:37,060 --> 01:26:40,000
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: in fact, humingi po kami ng supplemental na 700.

1372
01:26:40,580 --> 01:26:47,900
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: So, normally po, kung walang ganitong klaseng intensification of conflict,

1373
01:26:48,160 --> 01:26:52,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: we're already utilizing 60% of the 1.2 billion.

1374
01:26:52,260 --> 01:26:54,100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And this was spent on what, particularly?

1375
01:26:55,920 --> 01:26:56,900
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Um, if you...

1376
01:26:56,900 --> 01:26:58,720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Before the crisis po, no?

1377
01:26:58,800 --> 01:27:03,260
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Before the crisis, still the same repatriation expenses,

1378
01:27:03,380 --> 01:27:08,460
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: meaning international airfare, hotel or temporary accommodation,

1379
01:27:10,580 --> 01:27:16,900
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: medical escorts if needed, medical repatriation, land transportation,

1380
01:27:17,640 --> 01:27:22,000
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: domestic flight tickets, hotel accommodation here in the Philippines,

1381
01:27:22,300 --> 01:27:26,600
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: financial assistance for the repatriated workers,

1382
01:27:27,020 --> 01:27:28,740
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: and medical assistance.

1383
01:27:28,740 --> 01:27:30,560
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: If it's needed po.

1384
01:27:30,680 --> 01:27:35,140
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Karamihan po ng, Madam Chair, ng mga kaso prior to the crisis,

1385
01:27:35,420 --> 01:27:39,000
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ano po yung kaso ng mga ni-repatriate natin?

1386
01:27:39,000 --> 01:27:44,560
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Malaking porsyento po dito ang mga nawawalan po ng trabaho na ating mga kababayan,

1387
01:27:44,620 --> 01:27:45,420
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: distressed workers.

1388
01:27:45,420 --> 01:27:49,340
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ngunit ako na po ang unang aamin,

1389
01:27:49,540 --> 01:27:53,260
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: tumaas po ang medical repatriation din po natin.

1390
01:27:53,260 --> 01:27:58,580
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito po ang mga kababayan natin na hindi po natin puwedeng iwan abroad,

1391
01:27:58,580 --> 01:28:01,120
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: dahil may sakit sila.

1392
01:28:01,120 --> 01:28:04,660
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: So alam nyo naman po, pag medical repatriation, Madam Chair,

1393
01:28:04,880 --> 01:28:10,280
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: nire-require po minsan ng ospital or doktor na kailangan po may medical escort,

1394
01:28:10,540 --> 01:28:13,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ibig sabihin po nurse kasama sa aeroplano,

1395
01:28:13,380 --> 01:28:18,640
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: at minsan po pag, depende po sa attending physician,

1396
01:28:19,100 --> 01:28:26,020
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: sasabihin po nila baka kailangan nung ating worker ay tatlong upuan dahil hihiga po siya,

1397
01:28:26,040 --> 01:28:29,360
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: kung anong kailangan para maiuwi yung ating kababayan.

1398
01:28:29,400 --> 01:28:34,560
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: so this is also being paid by the emergency repatriation fund po.

1399
01:28:34,560 --> 01:28:42,160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ano pong sinabi ng DBM bakit nire-reduce nila yung inyong repatriation fund and yung NEP?

1400
01:28:44,360 --> 01:28:47,060
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Madam Chair, if I may po.

1401
01:28:47,140 --> 01:28:53,520
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: I believe that they're looking at utilization rate and the utilization rate of 2025.

1402
01:28:55,340 --> 01:28:57,980
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: However, the conflict arose,

1403
01:28:57,980 --> 01:29:01,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: starting Feb 28 of this year,

1404
01:29:01,180 --> 01:29:02,880
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: and it's still ongoing,

1405
01:29:02,880 --> 01:29:13,480
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: and this is, I would say, outside the control of the Department of Migrant Workers or OWWA.

1406
01:29:15,120 --> 01:29:27,320
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: The repatriation, emergency repatriation fund at ang action fund, ito po ay mga standby fund na pag at kung saka sakaling may,

1407
01:29:27,320 --> 01:29:30,020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, may I ask the Secretary,

1408
01:29:30,460 --> 01:29:36,020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: does DMW fully endorse the entire 2 billion request and commit to defend it through final congressional action?

1409
01:29:37,620 --> 01:29:39,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes, Mr. Congressman, Madam Chair.

1410
01:29:39,940 --> 01:29:45,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We stand by all our requests between the OWWA and the DMW.

1411
01:29:45,180 --> 01:29:47,620
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We share the same levels.

1412
01:29:49,300 --> 01:29:50,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We are joined at the hip.

1413
01:29:50,800 --> 01:29:54,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kaya po kami ay magkatuwang at

1414
01:29:54,140 --> 01:29:55,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: sabay po.

1415
01:29:55,780 --> 01:29:58,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes, the short answer is yes, we endorse this.

1416
01:29:58,580 --> 01:30:00,800
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, Mr. Secretary.

1417
01:30:01,100 --> 01:30:08,920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, I strongly object to using utilization rate mechanically as a reason to reduce the Emergency Repatriation Fund.

1418
01:30:09,200 --> 01:30:16,420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: We cannot predict when war, mass displacement, or evacuation will occur, but we can anticipate and prepare.

1419
01:30:16,420 --> 01:30:24,500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: A contingency fund does not become unnecessary simply because the worst crisis did not occur during a particular year.

1420
01:30:24,720 --> 01:30:30,820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: In any event, utilization is already high, as mentioned by Administrator Caunan's letter.

1421
01:30:31,600 --> 01:30:41,040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Sinabi po niya na 81.92% of the current fiscal year 2026 ERF appropriation has already been utilized as of July 31.

1422
01:30:41,040 --> 01:30:50,440
Rep. Roberto Nazal: The separate OWWA table submitted to us as of August 25 shows total ERF expenses at 1.6 billion,

1423
01:30:50,680 --> 01:30:54,100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: 663.284 million,

1424
01:30:54,100 --> 01:30:55,580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: for war-related expenses,

1425
01:30:55,860 --> 01:30:59,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and 967 million for regular repatriation.

1426
01:31:00,300 --> 01:31:02,360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, may I ask the Secretary,

1427
01:31:02,680 --> 01:31:08,180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: was the 24% reduction in ERF based wholly or partly on past utilization?

1428
01:31:08,180 --> 01:31:16,940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: If so, does the DMW agree that this is an unsafe basis for determining the required level of a life and safety contingency fund?

1429
01:31:17,580 --> 01:31:19,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: I can respond.

1430
01:31:19,560 --> 01:31:24,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: The numerics po, I think PY can perhaps respond to the details.

1431
01:31:24,600 --> 01:31:31,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But I can fully subscribe to the principle that utilization is a difficult basis.

1432
01:31:31,180 --> 01:31:40,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And having said that, utilization anyway will be dependent on the geopolitical situation.

1433
01:31:40,620 --> 01:31:47,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And as the February 28 US-Israel-Iran war had clearly proven,

1434
01:31:47,640 --> 01:31:51,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: any geopolitical crisis can happen anytime.

1435
01:31:52,630 --> 01:31:54,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: It will always be...

1436
01:31:54,220 --> 01:31:56,860
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: beyond our control in terms of the powers that be,

1437
01:31:57,000 --> 01:31:59,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: geopolitical powers that be.

1438
01:31:59,440 --> 01:32:02,860
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But, however, it is definitely within our control

1439
01:32:02,860 --> 01:32:08,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: to have the necessary resources ready to be mobilized when the time comes.

1440
01:32:08,460 --> 01:32:12,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And the President has clearly given us clear instructions

1441
01:32:12,700 --> 01:32:15,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: to have the necessary resources.

1442
01:32:15,860 --> 01:32:17,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ito pong pagbigay sa amin ng Pangulo

1443
01:32:17,820 --> 01:32:23,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ng 3 billion peso supplemental fund is a very, very clear statement

1444
01:32:23,400 --> 01:32:24,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: from no less than...

1445
01:32:24,360 --> 01:32:27,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: the President himself na napakahalaga ng resources.

1446
01:32:27,480 --> 01:32:31,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kaya for our part, Mr. Congressman, if I may speak also for the DMW,

1447
01:32:32,120 --> 01:32:35,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ang gusto rin naman na hoon naming level sa action fund namin

1448
01:32:35,780 --> 01:32:38,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: is 3 billion as set by the President himself.

1449
01:32:39,060 --> 01:32:41,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasi 2 billion lang hoon kami sa NEP.

1450
01:32:41,080 --> 01:32:46,640
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And then there are items din po to round up the 2 billion figure from the DMW side

1451
01:32:46,640 --> 01:32:51,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: that had already also been justified in our letter to the Speaker.

1452
01:32:51,740 --> 01:32:53,640
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, the short answer is,

1453
01:32:53,640 --> 01:32:56,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: tama po kayo, Mr. Congressman.

1454
01:32:56,520 --> 01:32:59,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: When it comes to crisis responses,

1455
01:32:59,540 --> 01:33:09,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: precisely, there is no crystal ball that will tell us when a crisis will occur.

1456
01:33:09,320 --> 01:33:14,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And so, we must be sure that there are resources always ready 100% of the time.

1457
01:33:14,540 --> 01:33:16,260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Natigil na po ba yung Middle East conflict?

1458
01:33:18,080 --> 01:33:23,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: I believe the political expert to conclude on this matter,

1459
01:33:23,900 --> 01:33:26,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Mr. Congressman.

1460
01:33:26,320 --> 01:33:33,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: However, we can say for ourselves that while there is a ceasefire,

1461
01:33:33,440 --> 01:33:38,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: there was a ceasefire, and it appears to be implemented at the present,

1462
01:33:39,700 --> 01:33:44,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: we can be sure, based on the incidents that happened 3 weeks ago,

1463
01:33:45,460 --> 01:33:50,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: that it may reignite or resume at any given time.

1464
01:33:51,320 --> 01:33:53,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: One side had attacked the other.

1465
01:33:53,600 --> 01:33:58,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And to retaliate, once again, we saw attacks in the Gulf states.

1466
01:33:59,700 --> 01:34:04,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: While we are so thankful to the Gulf states' host governments, countries,

1467
01:34:04,020 --> 01:34:09,480
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: for literally, through their defense systems, defending, protecting our workers, our people,

1468
01:34:10,420 --> 01:34:14,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: again, on the Philippine side, we must also be ready.

1469
01:34:14,860 --> 01:34:19,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: More than any other origin country, migrant worker origin country, Mr. Chair,

1470
01:34:19,840 --> 01:34:22,520
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: tayo po ang nag-respond for our citizens.

1471
01:34:22,880 --> 01:34:24,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And we want to keep it that way.

1472
01:34:25,720 --> 01:34:32,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We do not want to lose this opportunity to help our Filipinos in crisis.

1473
01:34:32,180 --> 01:34:36,380
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So basically, di pa natitigil ang krisis in the Middle East.

1474
01:34:36,820 --> 01:34:42,160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And I have to add that we must also prepare for a possible Taiwan-Strait conflict

1475
01:34:42,160 --> 01:34:44,640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: affecting nearly 200,000 Filipinos.

1476
01:34:45,180 --> 01:34:48,600
Rep. Roberto Nazal: The government already has contingency planning,

1477
01:34:48,600 --> 01:34:52,860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: but Congress must know whether the plan is fully costed and funded.

1478
01:34:54,060 --> 01:34:58,940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, there is also a risk of stricter or reciprocal immigration enforcement

1479
01:34:58,940 --> 01:35:00,880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: arising from our tensions with China.

1480
01:35:00,880 --> 01:35:04,720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: More than 100 Filipinos recently, based on reports po,

1481
01:35:04,820 --> 01:35:10,240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ang 100 Filipinos faced immigration action in China

1482
01:35:10,240 --> 01:35:14,380
Rep. Roberto Nazal: following the controversy over the Chinese nationals detained dito po sa Pilipinas.

1483
01:35:15,120 --> 01:35:18,180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, we cannot conclusively call this retaliation,

1484
01:35:18,320 --> 01:35:22,620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: but we cannot ignore the possibility of,

1485
01:35:22,620 --> 01:35:23,460
Rep. Roberto Nazal: tit-for-tat enforcement.

1486
01:35:24,460 --> 01:35:25,380
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Tama po ba?

1487
01:35:25,920 --> 01:35:28,500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Hong Kong has a separate immigration system,

1488
01:35:28,500 --> 01:35:33,720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: but it is strictly enforcing its prohibition against unauthorized second or part-time jobs.

1489
01:35:34,640 --> 01:35:38,500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Filipino workers have been arrested or jailed for illegal employment.

1490
01:35:39,500 --> 01:35:41,620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Marami po kasi kami nakausap sa Hong Kong eh.

1491
01:35:41,680 --> 01:35:44,160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Tapos ang sinasabi po nila, karamihan sa kanila,

1492
01:35:44,160 --> 01:35:46,040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: kumukuha ng pangalawa, pangatlong trabaho.

1493
01:35:46,440 --> 01:35:50,920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Noon, pinapayagan sila ng Hong Kong, pero ngayon, parang ang nangyayari,

1494
01:35:51,040 --> 01:35:52,740
Rep. Roberto Nazal: hinihigpitan po sila, dahil yata,

1495
01:35:52,740 --> 01:35:55,120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: mahigpit tayo sa mga Chinese workers dito.

1496
01:35:55,380 --> 01:36:00,960
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, whatever our position, our government position maintained towards China is,

1497
01:36:01,140 --> 01:36:06,120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: we must also fund the protection of OFWs who may bear the consequences.

1498
01:36:06,920 --> 01:36:08,900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, may I ask the Secretary,

1499
01:36:09,300 --> 01:36:13,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: how many Filipinos in China and Hong Kong presently have visa,

1500
01:36:13,440 --> 01:36:20,360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: are overstaying, or are unauthorized secondary, have secondary work problems?

1501
01:36:20,880 --> 01:36:27,720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And what would be the minimum ERF and WASP funding na kailangan

1502
01:36:27,720 --> 01:36:32,160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: for lawyers, detention visits, documentation, medical assistance, and repatriation?

1503
01:36:33,380 --> 01:36:39,620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And Madam Chair, what is the DMW's fully-costed evacuation plan for Filipinos in Taiwan

1504
01:36:39,620 --> 01:36:42,480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: if commercial air and sea routes are disrupted?

1505
01:36:43,320 --> 01:36:47,640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What minimum standby ERF is required so that the government can act immediately

1506
01:36:47,640 --> 01:36:50,180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: instead of waiting for a supplemental release

1507
01:36:50,180 --> 01:36:51,820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: after a crisis has already begun?

1508
01:36:54,520 --> 01:37:00,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Mr. Chair, we do have the figures of OFWs in both Hong Kong and China.

1509
01:37:01,940 --> 01:37:06,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: However, we do not have figures as to who are overstaying,

1510
01:37:06,860 --> 01:37:10,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: nor those who have secondary lines of work.

1511
01:37:11,240 --> 01:37:13,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: There would be difficulty gathering this data.

1512
01:37:13,940 --> 01:37:16,860
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But rest assured, over the weekend,

1513
01:37:17,100 --> 01:37:20,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: we just had an Undersecretary visit Hong Kong

1514
01:37:20,380 --> 01:37:22,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and meet with the Filipino community there

1515
01:37:22,580 --> 01:37:25,940
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: to assure the community of our support.

1516
01:37:27,040 --> 01:37:32,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And thus far, at this stage, Mr. Congressman,

1517
01:37:32,320 --> 01:37:42,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: we do not see any distress calls that are unusual in Hong Kong at this stage.

1518
01:37:42,460 --> 01:37:44,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Of course, there are OFWs who need to be helped.

1519
01:37:45,120 --> 01:37:47,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We have our Migrant Resource Center ready always

1520
01:37:47,800 --> 01:37:49,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: to help our OFWs there.

1521
01:37:50,040 --> 01:37:51,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We stand ready always.

1522
01:37:51,700 --> 01:37:53,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: As to how much will be needed,

1523
01:37:53,880 --> 01:37:56,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: we feel that, once again,

1524
01:37:56,380 --> 01:37:58,500
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: the three billion support of the President

1525
01:37:58,500 --> 01:38:01,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: really set the benchmark at the very least

1526
01:38:01,820 --> 01:38:04,000
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: of what should be provided to our Action Fund.

1527
01:38:04,100 --> 01:38:08,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kaya nga humihingi kami ng karagdagan din sa aming AKSYON Fund

1528
01:38:08,020 --> 01:38:10,920
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: so that magiging sapat po.

1529
01:38:11,120 --> 01:38:12,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: With respect to Taiwan,

1530
01:38:13,000 --> 01:38:14,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: for these last three years,

1531
01:38:14,900 --> 01:38:18,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: we have been meeting not just DMW and OWWA.

1532
01:38:18,440 --> 01:38:21,000
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: DMW, OWWA, and other relevant agencies

1533
01:38:21,000 --> 01:38:26,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: with respect to crisis management manuals and processes

1534
01:38:26,040 --> 01:38:30,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: in the event that a crisis emerges.

1535
01:38:31,220 --> 01:38:33,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Hindi ko lang po masabi yung exact details,

1536
01:38:33,720 --> 01:38:35,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: but rest assured, Mr. Congressman,

1537
01:38:35,480 --> 01:38:39,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: we can provide the crisis manuals that are in place

1538
01:38:39,260 --> 01:38:42,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Saan po makikita, ano ang transport modalities

1539
01:38:42,240 --> 01:38:45,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: kapag may nangyari in that part of the world.

1540
01:38:45,560 --> 01:38:49,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero hindi ko po ma-disclose yung detalya at this stage.

1541
01:38:49,160 --> 01:38:50,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: I hope you understand

1542
01:38:50,140 --> 01:38:52,940
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: for security and confidentiality reasons.

1543
01:38:52,940 --> 01:38:53,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But rest assured,

1544
01:38:53,980 --> 01:38:57,500
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: magtatatlong taon na po

1545
01:38:57,500 --> 01:39:00,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: kasi isa po ito sa maagang instructions

1546
01:39:00,680 --> 01:39:01,860
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ng ating Pangulo

1547
01:39:01,860 --> 01:39:04,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: na umupo kami as a whole-of-government

1548
01:39:04,420 --> 01:39:07,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: aid entity endeavor

1549
01:39:09,020 --> 01:39:10,860
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: para handa po tayo

1550
01:39:10,860 --> 01:39:13,000
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: kapag nagka-crisis sa Taiwan.

1551
01:39:14,340 --> 01:39:15,420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair,

1552
01:39:15,560 --> 01:39:17,840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: just a last question.

1553
01:39:18,880 --> 01:39:22,400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kung sakali po na maubos ang pondo niyo,

1554
01:39:22,460 --> 01:39:24,100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: tapos biglang nagkaroon ng crisis,

1555
01:39:25,300 --> 01:39:28,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ganong katagal po ba ang tingin niyo?

1556
01:39:29,940 --> 01:39:30,660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Halimbawa,

1557
01:39:30,700 --> 01:39:32,380
Rep. Roberto Nazal: nagpasa pa ng supplemental budget

1558
01:39:32,380 --> 01:39:34,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: para magkaroon kayo ng additional funding,

1559
01:39:35,100 --> 01:39:37,160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ganong katagal ang magiging response niyo

1560
01:39:37,160 --> 01:39:39,680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: kung nagkaroon ng gera sa Taiwan?

1561
01:39:41,580 --> 01:39:44,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sa tingin ko po, dahil nga sa paghahanda namin

1562
01:39:44,800 --> 01:39:46,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: itong huling tatlong taon

1563
01:39:46,460 --> 01:39:48,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ay magiging maagap po ito.

1564
01:39:48,280 --> 01:39:50,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Again, this is an inter-agency effort.

1565
01:39:51,280 --> 01:39:53,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Of course, geographically,

1566
01:39:53,180 --> 01:39:55,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: malapit ang Taiwan.

1567
01:39:55,380 --> 01:39:58,920
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So the logistics will not be as difficult, say,

1568
01:39:59,020 --> 01:40:01,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: as a repatriation effort from the Middle East.

1569
01:40:02,440 --> 01:40:03,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And then, of course,

1570
01:40:03,860 --> 01:40:07,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: merong other government agencies involved.

1571
01:40:08,180 --> 01:40:14,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We can disclose this perhaps in confidence.

1572
01:40:14,360 --> 01:40:16,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Hindi ko lang po ma-disclose yung precise

1573
01:40:16,720 --> 01:40:20,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: appointed actions

1574
01:40:20,680 --> 01:40:24,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ng bawat government agency.

1575
01:40:24,260 --> 01:40:26,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But rest assured po,

1576
01:40:26,160 --> 01:40:28,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: based on the instructions of the President,

1577
01:40:28,360 --> 01:40:29,200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: we have been meeting

1578
01:40:29,200 --> 01:40:31,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and are prepared for this.

1579
01:40:31,500 --> 01:40:33,640
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And our response time will be swift

1580
01:40:33,640 --> 01:40:36,200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: kasi nga po may mga crisis manuals in place na po.

1581
01:40:36,200 --> 01:40:39,080
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kahit po maubos ang pondo ninyo, Madam Chair?

1582
01:40:39,300 --> 01:40:43,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kung maubos ang pondo natin,

1583
01:40:43,480 --> 01:40:45,240
