3632
03:36:31,580 --> 03:36:38,540
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: And then, of course, the extension for the training center and yung iba pa po nating facilities for Region 2.

3633
03:36:42,220 --> 03:36:44,980
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: The Seafarer Welfare Center, sir.

3634
03:36:44,980 --> 03:36:48,260
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: And the new office, sabi po ni Eugene.

3635
03:36:50,490 --> 03:36:55,080
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Number 4 po, Madam Chair, dear Congressman,

3636
03:36:55,640 --> 03:36:58,720
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: I invite you to reminisce a little bit.

3637
03:36:58,900 --> 03:37:07,760
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: RA 8042-1995, the Congress created a program called the Congressional Migrant Worker Scholarship Program.

3638
03:37:09,580 --> 03:37:20,460
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: But at that time, it was funded by PCSO, 150 million and 50 million from the CDF back then.

3639
03:37:20,660 --> 03:37:25,840
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: But from that time until now, wala na pong naging restoration of this budget.

3640
03:37:27,000 --> 03:37:32,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: This is supporting po, not just dependents, but also OFWs themselves.

3641
03:37:32,720 --> 03:37:36,280
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Up to 60,000 po a year ang binibigay for 4 years.

3642
03:37:36,580 --> 03:37:37,940
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Malaki pong tulong ito.

3643
03:37:37,940 --> 03:37:47,300
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito po ay compared to the regular scholarship program of OWWA, which is sourced from the trust fund, the private trust fund of OWWA.

3644
03:37:47,300 --> 03:37:48,760
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ito po ay GAA-sourced.

3645
03:37:49,260 --> 03:37:55,080
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Dito po ay pwede nating i-open up at maging mas accessible.

3646
03:37:55,600 --> 03:38:03,380
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ang scholarship para po sa ating pong mga kababayan, marami po talaga ang humihingi ng tulong, Madam Chair,

3647
03:38:03,620 --> 03:38:08,640
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: sa pagpapaaral ng kanilang mga anak at syempre sa sarili po rin nila.

3648
03:38:08,640 --> 03:38:13,060
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: With that po, our total is at 2 billion pesos.

3649
03:38:13,220 --> 03:38:16,520
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Again, MOOE gas at 322 million.

3650
03:38:16,840 --> 03:38:20,620
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: MOOE operations at 1.18 billion.

3651
03:38:21,040 --> 03:38:25,320
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Capital outlay at 447.99 million.

3652
03:38:25,440 --> 03:38:30,540
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: And the Congressional Migrant Workers Scholarship Program at an additional 50 million.

3653
03:38:30,720 --> 03:38:32,120
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Thank you very much, Madam Chair, dear Congressman.

3654
03:38:32,120 --> 03:38:33,980
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, PY Caunan.

3655
03:38:34,040 --> 03:38:44,180
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Before I would move for the approval of the increase of 2 billion each, I would like to just state I have here a constituent.

3656
03:38:44,360 --> 03:38:52,620
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The problem in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, there is the non-issuance of resident permit, ICAMA.

3657
03:38:52,920 --> 03:38:54,600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Could you explain this one first?

3658
03:38:54,600 --> 03:39:01,960
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What is this ICAMA not issued by the government of the Kingdom?

3659
03:39:01,960 --> 03:39:09,600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Who should be able to have our residents there work and transact business?

3660
03:39:10,220 --> 03:39:15,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes, in general po, this is required for every OFW who goes there.

3661
03:39:15,340 --> 03:39:18,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So every OFW has what you call an ICAMA, residence permit.

3662
03:39:19,600 --> 03:39:24,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: However, it can happen na nagkakaroon ng legal problems.

3663
03:39:24,600 --> 03:39:38,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ang mga kababayan natin, most likely related sa kanilang stay, maaring nag-overstay, o di kaya perceived violations of their stay.

3664
03:39:39,770 --> 03:39:45,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, ang key po dito, in brief, Mr. Chair, is the legal assistance through the AKSYON Fund.

3665
03:39:45,980 --> 03:39:53,940
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, the good news is kami ni Usec. Jun Rasul just came from Jeddah and we met our lawyers in Saudi.

3666
03:39:54,600 --> 03:40:05,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: The Tebiah Law Office who provides legal assistance, they have an array of 30 lawyers in their law firm who provide assistance to our workers.

3667
03:40:05,860 --> 03:40:17,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, we easily refer these cases na hindi maka-renew ng ICAMA for immigration-related problems or labor-related problems one way or another.

3668
03:40:17,900 --> 03:40:20,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, rest assured that we address this situation.

3669
03:40:20,680 --> 03:40:23,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Some cases take longer than others, admittedly.

3670
03:40:23,880 --> 03:40:37,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But rest assured, Mr. Congressman, Madam Chair, we are on top of the legal cases that are being handled by our law firm, our legal retainers, our in-house lawyers.

3671
03:40:38,160 --> 03:40:49,540
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And also, kung merong utang po, halimbawa, sa ospital or immigration-related penalties, we shoulder these expenses for our workers.

3672
03:40:50,680 --> 03:40:53,400
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Madam Chair.

3673
03:40:54,300 --> 03:41:04,500
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I now move for the approval of the budget of the DMW and the OWWA, plus 2 billion each.

3674
03:41:05,820 --> 03:41:12,360
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Because we have to convince the Speaker and our Chairperson that this is a department which should all help.

3675
03:41:12,520 --> 03:41:16,020
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: After all, we call our workers, overseas workers, our heroes.

3676
03:41:16,360 --> 03:41:19,160
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And so, we should be able to work on that.

3677
03:41:19,160 --> 03:41:21,460
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, with our Chair, we will be able to do that.

3678
03:41:21,460 --> 03:41:23,060
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, move, Madam Chair.

3679
03:41:23,060 --> 03:41:30,600
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Thank you so much, Honorable Rufus Rodriguez.

3680
03:41:30,600 --> 03:41:38,540
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Though we very much appreciate the motion, we want to remind everyone that this is, our proceeding today is just a budget briefing.

3681
03:41:38,540 --> 03:41:47,180
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: And, of course, the ruling would be considered in the proper time.

3682
03:41:47,300 --> 03:41:47,680
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Proper time.

3683
03:41:47,840 --> 03:41:48,180
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Yes.

3684
03:41:48,300 --> 03:41:49,360
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

3685
03:41:49,480 --> 03:41:50,120
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Thank you.

3686
03:41:50,920 --> 03:41:53,320
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Thank you so much, Honorable Rufus Rodriguez.

3687
03:41:53,340 --> 03:41:56,860
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Not just for your questions, but also for giving.

3688
03:41:56,860 --> 03:41:57,900
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: life to this proceeding.

3689
03:42:00,180 --> 03:42:03,680
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: Even Secretary Hans was excited to answer your questions.

3690
03:42:06,760 --> 03:42:09,840
Rep. Irene G. Labadlabad: I guess now we move on to our next interpolator.

